window.MONARCH_CHAPTERS=(window.MONARCH_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":301,"title":"Chapter 301: Monarch Of Destruction [2]","paragraphs":["Black energy erupted from his skin","RUMBLE.","His muscles expanded. His bones started to shift. His entire body began growing at an impossible rate.","Black scales emerged across his skin. His arms transformed into enormous clawed limbs.","His legs twisted and lengthened. His spine extended. A colossal tail emerged behind him.","Two enormous horns pushed from his skull.","His face elongated into the terrifying visage of a dragon.","BOOOOOOM!!!","A wave of black energy exploded through space. The transformation was complete.","A colossal dragon floated above the planet. Its scales were darker than the void itself, absorbing much of the distant starlight.","Its enormous horns curved backward from its skull.","Its eyes burned with a deep crimson radiance. Every movement caused space around its body to distort.","Then it continued growing larger and larger.","The planet beneath it suddenly seemed insignificant. The dragon’s body expanded until its enormous silhouette stretched farther than the maroon world below.","Its claws alone were large enough to crush mountains. Its wings unfolded.","WHOOOOOOOOOSH!","The resulting windstorm swept across the planet, completely dispersing the surrounding sandstorms.","The Monarch of Destruction had revealed his true form. And he was larger than the planet itself.","For a while, neither Monarch moved.","The Monarch of Decay stared upward.","Its rage was accompanied by caution.","The black dragon slowly lowered its enormous head. Crimson eyes focused upon the creature before him.","When he spoke, his voice no longer belonged to a human. It was the voice of something ancient. Something that had existed long before civilizations.","\"You have made one mistake, that is coming here.\"","The Monarch of Decay’s enormous eye narrowed. The black dragon continued.","\"You thought I planned everything to damage your soul... then you are wrong. To defeat you...\"","Black energy began gathering around his colossal body. The surrounding stars seemed to dim.","\"I don’t need a plan.\"","His enormous jaws slowly opened. Darkness gathered inside his mouth. The Monarch of Decay’s expression changed.","\"You... became stronger than last time I saw you.\" Monarch of decay spoke is worry.","The dragon’s voice echoed across space.","\"The things that happened there were not what i was expecting... still I got the same result...\"","His crimson eyes burned brighter.","\"And you are truly coward.. even now you came here not in your true form.\"","The Monarch of Decay roared.","\"DIE!\"","Countless tentacles surged through space.","The black dragon spread his enormous wings.","And for one brief moment. The universe between the two Monarchs became completely silent.","Then both moved.","BOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOM!!!","Their powers collided. The shockwave spread across the void like an expanding wall, shaking the maroon planet beneath them and scattering enormous clouds of crimson dust into space.","Two ancient existences collided in the depths of space. The very moment their powers met, the surrounding void seemed to tremble.","BOOOOOOM!!!","A colossal shockwave erupted from the point of impact.","It expanded through space for thousands of kilometers, tearing apart asteroids and reducing smaller celestial bodies to fragments.","Distant stars flickered violently as waves of destructive energy washed over them.","Black light clashed against crimson.","BOOM!","BOOM!","BOOOOOOM!!!","The Monarch of Decay unleashed countless tendrils of corrupted energy, each one capable of tearing through mountains and consuming entire regions of land.","But against the Monarch of Destruction, they were not enough.","They both possessed different abilities and authority that could destroy worlds. But against each other they didn’t work well.","The enormous black dragon moved through space with terrifying speed.","His claws tore through the darkness, each strike carrying enough destructive force to distort space itself.","The Monarch of Decay attempted to counterattack.","Its countless tentacles surged forward from every direction.","The dragon simply swept one enormous claw across them.","SHRRRRRAAAK!!!","Hundreds of tentacles were severed simultaneously.","The corrupted energy was no threat to him nor it have any effect on his body.","While black color of destructive energy spread across the wounds, preventing them from immediately regenerating.","The Monarch of Decay roared.","\"YOU THINK YOU CAN DEFEAT ME?!\"","Its enormous body expanded.","More flesh emerged from its torso. Countless mouths opened across its body, releasing waves of corrupted energy.","The surrounding space began to decay. Even the distant light of stars seemed to fade as the corruption spread.","Yet the Monarch of Destruction remained unmoved.","He accelerated.","BOOM!","His enormous body disappeared.","CRAAAAASH!!!","His claw slammed directly into the Monarch of Decay.","The impact sent the gigantic abomination flying through space.","Its enormous body crashed through an asteroid belt, completely destroying thousands of rocks in its path.","Before it could recover, the black dragon was already above it.","The Monarch of Decay looked upward. Something resembling fear appeared within its countless eyes.","The dragon’s enormous jaws slowly opened.","Silence fell.","Then energy began gathering inside his mouth. At first, it was only a small point of light.","Then it expanded. Brilliant crimson energy accumulated between his jaws, becoming brighter and brighter until it illuminated the surrounding void.","Space itself began to distort around it.","The Monarch of Decay immediately understood.","\"No...\"","The dragon’s eyes burned with absolute indifference. The energy reached its peak.","\"NO!\"","The Monarch of Decay desperately released every ounce of power it possessed. Countless tentacles formed a gigantic barrier around its body.","Mouths opened across its flesh. Corrupted energy erupted in every direction.","But the dragon had already made his decision.","His jaws opened wider.","ROOOOOOOOOOOOOAAAAAAR!!!","A colossal beam of destructive energy erupted from his mouth.","BOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOM!!!","The beam swallowed the darkness.","It was so enormous that its width alone stretched across countless kilometers.","The entire body of the Monarch of Decay disappeared inside it.","The corrupted barriers were destroyed instantly.","Tentacles vaporized. Rotten flesh was erased. Its countless mouths screamed simultaneously as the destructive beam consumed everything around it.","The beam didn’t stop.","It continued forward through the void. It tore through several enormous asteroids, reducing them to dust.","A distant planet caught the edge of the attack.","BOOOOOOM!!!","Its surface was instantly obliterated. The beam continued farther. Another celestial body disappeared.","Even distant stars were engulfed by the crimson radiance, their light swallowed beneath the overwhelming destructive force.","The beam continued tearing through space.","The crimson light gradually faded. The surrounding darkness returned. Nothing remained where the Monarch of Decay had been.","Only drifting fragments of matter remained scattered throughout the void.","The black dragon hovered silently. His enormous wings slowly moved through the vacuum.","He stared at the empty space before him. There was no celebration. No roar of victory. Nor an expression of satisfaction.","Only cold silence. After a moment, his enormous crimson eyes narrowed.","\"He was really weakened... just because his soul was slightly damaged.\" The dragon commented on Decay.","His gaze drifted toward the distant stars.","\"Everything went differently.\"","A low growl escaped his throat.","\"But now...\"","His thoughts returned to the young man who had somehow survived the Monarch of Decay.","The human carrying the Moon Goddess’s divine power.","The human possessing the bloodline of a Monarch. Which Monarch? He didn’t know.","The dragon’s expression became unreadable.","He remained there alone in the endless darkness.","Around him, the remnants of their battle slowly drifted through space."]},{"number":302,"title":"Chapter 302: Waking up","paragraphs":["The forest was eerily quiet.","This was the same place where Noah and Damien had entered the labyrinth months ago. The hill inside the forest where the entrance had once stood at base.","But the hill was gone. There was no trace of the labyrinth anymore.","Instead, a large clearing had appeared in the middle of the forest. Broken trees surrounded the area, and the ground was littered with the bodies of countless monsters.","Their pale, oily skin had lost its unnatural shine. They lay completely motionless, their bodies lifeless.","Near the edge of the clearing, beneath the shade of a large tree, someone was sitting.","It was Akari.","Her kimono was badly torn, and several parts of her skin were blackened and damaged.","Some areas of her cheek and arms still showed the terrible effects of the corruption that had touched her.","Yet she was alive. Her eyes were open, and her breathing had finally returned to normal.","Resting comfortably on her lap was Noah.","His snow-white hair fell smoothly across her thighs. His breathing was steady, and there wasn’t a single trace of injury or corruption on his body.","He looked completely unharmed.","It was almost impossible to believe that he had just survived an encounter with such a terrifying creature.","Akari gently brushed a few strands of his hair away from his forehead.","Then she raised her eyes toward the woman standing several meters away.","The woman was leaning casually against a tree.","She had long, silver-white hair, the ends of which gradually shifted into a brilliant orange, resembling flames. Her skin was fair and flawless, while her eyes possessed an unusual fiery glow.","Akari studied her carefully.","\"Who are you?\" she asked. \"And how did you get there? How did you save us?\"","The woman was looking at Noah for a while now, before looking back at Akari.","\"My name is Sefira.\"","She straightened slightly from the tree.","\"And since you asked what I am... you already saw the answer.\"","Her fiery eyes narrowed slightly.","\"I’m not human.\"","A faint smile appeared on her lips.","\"I’m a Phoenix.\"","Akari’s expression became slightly more serious.","\"A Phoenix...\"","She had heard of creatures like them, but meeting one was an entirely different matter.","Phoenixes were just like dragons. They existed in stories and considered as mythical beings similar to dragons.","\"But how did you find us?\" Akari asked. \"And how did you manage to save us from that place?\"","Sefira folded her arms.","\"Honestly? You two were lucky.\"","\"Lucky?\"","\"Yes.\"","Sefira glanced toward the clearing.","\"I was investigating a portal that had appeared in this forest. Monsters were constantly coming through it, so I entered the portal to find its source and stop them. It led me inside a labyrinth. \"","She paused for a moment.","\"But while I was inside, another portal suddenly appeared.\"","Akari frowned.","\"Another portal?\"","\"I didn’t know where it led. I had no idea what was on the other side.\"","Sefira’s expression became slightly more serious.","\"But I decided to enter anyway.\"","She looked directly at Akari.","\"That’s when I found you two.\"","Akari listened silently.","\"You were falling from the sky,\" Sefira continued. \"Both of you looked like you were barely alive. I caught you before you hit the ground and brought you back here.\"","Akari lowered her gaze toward Noah.","She still remembered what had happened.","She looked back at Sefira.","\"What about the portal?\"","\"Which one?\"","\"The portal inside the labyrinth. And the labyrinth itself.\"","Sefira remained silent for a few seconds.","Then she shook her head.","\"It’s gone.\"","Akari’s eyes narrowed.","\"Gone?\"","\"It disappeared shortly after we came out.\"","Sefira pointed toward the surrounding clearing.","\"And something else happened.\"","Akari followed her gaze.","\"All those monsters suddenly died.\"","Only then did Akari properly examine the clearing.","Hundreds of the strange creatures were scattered across the ground.","Their bodies were unmistakable.","The same pale, oily-skinned monsters that had surrounded the abomination were now lying dead.","There wasn’t a single one still moving.","Akari’s expression became solemn.","\"Those are the same creatures that came from the portal.\"","\"Exactly,\" Sefira replied.","Akari gently ran her fingers through Noah’s hair.","Her mind was filled with questions. None of it made sense.","Sefira noticed her troubled expression.","\"You seem to have a lot of questions.\"","Akari looked at her.","\"I do.\"","Sefira smiled faintly.","\"Then we’re probably going to have a long conversation.\"","Akari nodded.","But before she could say anything else, Noah shifted slightly in her lap.","Both women immediately looked down at him.","His eyelids trembled.","Akari’s expression softened.","\"Noah...?\"","While Sefira stiffened. She looked around as if she didn’t know whether to stay here or just leave this two.","She pressed her lips. Then said, \"For now I am going... I will meet you... two when you both are recovered.\"","Akari tried to stop her. \"Wait–\"","But before she could speak further, Sefira vanished.","---","Sefira appeared several kilometers away from the clearing, standing alone among the trees.","She let out a quiet sigh.","\"I need to tell Noah the truth about Mary...\"","Her expression became complicated.","\"But I ran away before I could say anything. Damn it.\"","She rubbed her forehead before looking back toward the distant clearing.","\"Well, we need to talk when we’re alone. I’ll tell him next time.\"","Sefira reached into her storage ring and took out a small communication device.","She activated it. The device rang for a few seconds before someone finally answered.","\"I found Noah,\" Sefira said calmly. \"Go to the place where the labyrinth was. All the monsters there are dead.\"","Silence came from the other end. Then a trembling voice finally replied.","\"R-Really? You found Noah?\"","\"Yes. He’s alive.\"","A relieved breath came through the device.","\"T-Thank you...\"","The voice became softer.","\"Thank you so much. I don’t know how I can ever repay you.\"","\"Don’t thank me,\" Sefira replied. \"You did plenty of work yourself. Besides, you haven’t forgotten our agreement, have you?\"","There was a brief pause.","\"No. I remember.\"","\"Good. When the time comes, you still have to do what I ask, Morgana.\"","\"I will,\" Morgana answered quietly. \"You have my word.\"","The communication ended. Sefira lowered the device and returned it to her storage ring.","She glanced once more toward the direction of the clearing.","\"I should head back to the base.\"","A faint smile appeared on her face.","\"Noah is finally safe.\"","She felt relieved.","After everything that had happened, seeing him alive and seemingly unharmed had been enough to ease some of the tension she had been carrying.","She had disappeared before Noah woke up.","She wasn’t entirely sure why. Perhaps she had simply felt nervous about facing him.","\"That was strange.\"","A male voice suddenly came from above.","\"Why did you run away?\"","Sefira froze.","\"You should have stayed there and proudly announced, ’Noah. I’m the one who saved you.’\"","She slowly raised her head.","A man was sitting casually on a thick tree branch several meters above her.","His legs dangled freely from the branch. He wore completely black clothing and a dark mask that concealed most of his face.","Sefira’s eyes narrowed. A","\"Shadow...\"","The masked man tilted his head slightly.","\"That’s right.\"","His voice carried a hint of amusement."]},{"number":303,"title":"Chapter 303: Don’t Ask Me How I Know All Of This","paragraphs":["\"Hehe~ Yup, it’s me, Shadow.\" The man chuckled.","Sefira remained cautious. Her eyes stayed fixed on the masked man.","\"How did you do that?\" she asked. \"How did you know where Noah was? And how did you open that portal?\"","The man looked at her. Although his face was hidden behind the mask, Sefira could somehow tell that he was smiling. He casually jumped down from the tree.","Thud!","His feet touched the ground without making much of an impact.","\"Our deal was simple,\" Shadow said. \"I help you, and in return, you help me when the time comes.\"","He took a few steps toward her.","\"But I never agreed to explain how I knew where Noah was, where he had disappeared to, or how I managed to open a portal to that exact location.\"","Sefira’s expression tightened.","Shadow continued.","\"Just like the deal you made with that Morgana girl, I made a deal with you.\"","He sighed.","\"Some things are better left unanswered.\"","Sefira pressed her lips into a thin line. She was strong—undeniably so. Yet the man standing before her was on an entirely different level.","She could sense it simply by being near him.","His presence alone was enough to make her instincts remain on edge.","She still remembered how they had met.","Shadow had appeared out of nowhere and claimed that he could help her find Noah.","At first, Sefira had been extremely cautious.","Noah had been missing for nearly a month, and despite everything she had tried, she hadn’t been able to locate him.","Then Shadow appeared. He claimed to know where Noah was. More importantly, Sefira quickly realized that he was far stronger than her.","That was the reason she had eventually accepted his offer. They had come to this very forest.","Shadow had simply raised one hand and opened a mysterious portal with a casual wave.","Sefira had been stunned. But what shocked her even more was what came next. He had known about her true identity. He had instructed her to enter the portal in her Phoenix form.","He knew far too much. And yet, despite all her questions, he had never given her a proper answer.","\"Don’t be so tense, Sefira,\" Shadow said casually. \"For now, go back home and get some rest.\"","He turned slightly away from her.","\"As for who I am...\"","A faint chuckle escaped him.","\"You’ll find that out eventually.\"","Sefira sighed.","\"You...\"","She rubbed her forehead.","\"I have so many questions about you, but I’ve already realized that I’m probably never going to get straight answers.\"","She looked directly at him. \"So I won’t ask about your identity.\"","Her expression became serious.","\"But at least tell me this.\"","Shadow glanced back at her.","\"Where was Noah?\"","Sefira paused before asking the question that had been bothering her even more.","\"And where was Akari for the last twelve years?\"","Her voice became quieter.","\"What happened to them? What did they encounter?\"","For a moment, Shadow remained silent.","Then he nodded.","\"Well...\"","He turned to face her completely.","\"I suppose that’s something I can answer right now.\"","Sefira’s expression became serious as she waited for him to continue.","\"Akari was trapped inside an unknown realm by an ancient dragon,\" Shadow explained. \"The dragon had a purpose for doing so. It wanted her to awaken her dormant dragon bloodline.\"","Sefira’s eyes narrowed. \"An ancient dragon...?\"","Shadow ignored her question and continued.","\"When Akari finally awakened her bloodline, however, something unexpected happened. The Monarch of Decay entered that realm.\"","\"The Monarch of Decay?\" Sefira repeated, her expression shocked, the word Monarch send shivers down her spine.","Shadow nodded. \"The last Storm Dragon was his greatest enemy. He hated that dragon more than almost anything else. So, when he sensed the awakening of a new Storm Dragon, he naturally wanted to kill her as well.\"","Sefira remained silent, listening carefully.","\"But things didn’t go as he expected.\"","A faint smile appeared on Shadow’s face.","\"That puppet of the Monarch of Decay was ultimately defeated by both Noah and Akari.\"","Sefira’s eyes widened slightly.","\"Both of them... defeated it?\"","\"Yes.\"","Shadow folded his arms.","\"Honestly, once Akari had fully awakened her bloodline and they defeated the Monarch’s puppet, the two of them should have been able to escape that realm and return to the real world without much difficulty.\"","He paused.","\"Unfortunately...\"","His expression became slightly more serious.","\"The puppet was far stronger than expected. The battle between it, Noah, and Akari became so destructive that the entire realm was eventually torn apart.\"","Sefira’s expression changed.","\"Torn apart?\"","\"Yes. The realm itself could no longer withstand their clash.\"","Shadow looked toward the distant forest.","\"It was completely destroyed and ceased to exist.\"","Sefira remained silent for a moment, trying to process everything she had just heard.","\"So Noah and Akari...\"","\"They survived,\" Shadow interrupted calmly. \"Barely.\"","He then looked back at her.","\"That is why I decided to help them.\"","Sefira frowned.","\"You?\"","Shadow gave a small shrug.","\"I told you before. I had my reasons.\"","He paused before continuing.","\"I informed you of their location because I knew you would eventually find them and help them. In return, you’ll help me with something in the future.\"","Sefira stared at him. \"So that was our deal...\"","\"Exactly.\"","Shadow smiled faintly.","\"Although, don’t ask me how I know all of this.\"","Sefira’s eyes narrowed. \"You really are...\" She paused.","\"Hehe~.\" Shadow simply chuckled.","\"As for the remaining details, you can ask Noah or Akari yourself once they’re awake. They can tell you what happened from their perspective.\"","He turned away from her.","\"That’s all I can tell you for now. Now, bye~ bye~\"","\"Wait—\"","Sefira suddenly stepped forward.","But before she could say anything else, Shadow’s body began to distort. His form melted into darkness, flowing like liquid shadow.","\"Take care of them, Sefira.\"","His voice echoed through the clearing.","\"And don’t worry too much. You’ll learn who I am eventually.\"","The next instant, his entire body dissolved into shadow and vanished without leaving a trace.","Sefira stood there silently.","She stared at the empty branch where Shadow had been sitting only moments ago.","\"...That man.\"","She sighed helplessly.","\"He’s hiding far too many secrets.\""]},{"number":304,"title":"Chapter 304: Not your fault","paragraphs":["\"Argh...!\"","Noah’s eyelids twitched as he struggled to open them.","His entire body felt numb.","It was as if he had completely lost control over his limbs. He tried to move his fingers, but they refused to respond. Even lifting his head felt impossible.","’What’s happening...?’","His thoughts were sluggish, drifting in and out of consciousness.","Then he heard voices. Two people were talking nearby. Their voices sounded strangely familiar, but his mind was too hazy to identify them.","’Is that... Akari?’","A sudden worry surfaced within him.","’Is she okay?’","He tried to focus on the conversation, but the voices gradually became distant. His consciousness began slipping away again.","’Akari...’","Before he could gather another thought, darkness swallowed his mind.","---","Blink.","Blink.","Noah’s eyelids slowly opened. The first thing he saw was a beautiful ceiling.","’Damn...’","He stared at it for several seconds, trying to understand where he was.","Strangely, he felt no pain. However, his entire body was still exhausted, as though he had been drained of every ounce of strength.","\"I am... safe,\" he muttered quietly.","His voice was hoarse.","Noah slowly turned his head.","That was when he noticed the chamber around him.","It was spacious and elegantly furnished, with refined wooden walls and expensive-looking decorations. Soft evening light streamed through the large window, casting a warm golden glow across the room.","The sight immediately reminded him of a noble manor.","’Wait...’","His eyes widened slightly.","’This isn’t the world I was trapped in.... That means... I’m back.’","The place he was currently at didn’t look like hospital nor did it look like a temple. It looked like a private chamber inside a massive estate.","For a moment, relief washed over him. But it disappeared almost immediately.","\"Where is Akari...?\"","His voice carried a hint of panic. She wasn’t here. Noah immediately tried to sit up, but his exhausted body barely responded.","Just then, \"You are awake?\"","A familiar female voice came from beside the bed.","Noah turned his head.","A woman with sky-blue hair was sitting beside him on a chair. Her violet eyes watched at him.","He recognized her immediately.","\"Instructor Morgana?\"","It was his instructor from Novaris Academy.","Morgana looked at him with a gentle expression.","Noah’s concern returned almost instantly.","\"Instructor Morgana, where is Akari?\"","\"Calm down. She’s fine.\" She was little surprised seeing how much worried Noah was for Akari.","Hearing those words, Noah finally relaxed.","\"Where is she?\"","Morgana looked at him for a moment before answering.","\"She’s back in this world. Where else do you think she would be right now?\"","Noah’s eyes widened slightly. Then realization dawned on him.","\"Ah...\"","He slowly nodded.","\"Yes... She must have gone to meet her family.\"","A relieved sigh escaped his lips as he closed his eyes. At least Akari had made it back safely with him.","Morgana watched him relax. However, her expression soon became filled with guilt.","\"I’m sorry, Noah.\"","He opened his eyes again.","Morgana lowered her gaze.","\"Again and again, I keep failing as an instructor. Once more, because of me, Damien and especially you—had to face something so dangerous. This time Damien didn’t face much danger, but you did.\"","Noah stared at her. For a moment, he was confused.","Then he understood what she meant. He knew this world was supposed to be base on a game. A world where the story had already been written. The future was set.","Damien was destined to face countless dangers. And more often than not, no one arrived in time to save him.","Not because those people were incompetent. Not because they were weak. It was simply because that was how the story had been written.","They were never meant to arrive in time. They were never meant to prevent every disaster.","They had their own problems to deal with while the events of the world unfolded according to a predetermined path.","Noah looked at Morgana’s guilty expression and smiled faintly.","\"You are not at fault, Instructor.\"","Morgana raised her eyes.","\"It’s not like you knew what was going to happen, where it would happen, or when it would happen. So please, don’t blame yourself.\"","He paused before giving her a playful smile.","\"Besides, I’m much happier about being able to see you again after such a long time. I really missed you.\"","His smile widened. \"So please don’t make such a sad face. Hehe~\"","Morgana stared at him for a few seconds. Then, despite herself, a small smile appeared on her face.","\"You really know how to say sweet things, Noah.\"","\"Of course I do.\" Noah proudly raised his chin.","Morgana shook her head with a faint chuckle before standing from her chair.","\"I’ll go and inform Lady Akari that you’ve awakened. You should continue resting.\"","She walked toward the door.","\"If you need anything, tell the servant standing outside.\"","Noah nodded.","\"Understood.\"","But before Morgana could leave, he suddenly remembered something.","\"Wait.\"","She turned around.","\"Where exactly are we?\"","Noah glanced around the elegant chamber.","\"This doesn’t look like a hospital or a temple. It’s more like a chamber inside some enormous mansion.\"","Morgana nodded.","\"That’s because it is.\"","She looked at him.","\"We’re currently at the Thornveil Household.\"","Noah’s eyes widened.","\"The Thornveil Household?\"","’Well... that actually makes sense.’","Considering where everything had happened, there weren’t many other places where they could have brought him.","Morgana noticed his surprised expression and smiled reassuringly.","\"Don’t worry. No one here is going to harm you.\"","She opened the door.","\"I’ll come back later. Until then, get some rest. Though I am very curious as where Lady Akari was for last twelve years, and how you were with her. I will just ask about it later.\"","Noah nodded.","\"Okay, Instructor.\"","Morgana left the chamber, closing the door behind her.","Silence once again settled over the room.","Noah remained alone on the bed, staring at the warm evening sunlight spilling through the window.","Finally, after spending nearly seven months in that realm, he was outside. Now he could finally breathe peacefully."]},{"number":305,"title":"Chapter 305: A request?","paragraphs":["Noah stood before the mirror, tilting his head slightly to the left. Then to the right. He examined his reflection for a few seconds.","\"Guess my charm increased once again...\"","He reached up and gently caressed his own cheek, admiring his reflection.","Yet despite his handsome appearance, there was an unmistakable look of dissatisfaction on his face.","’What’s the use of having such a handsome face when I’m still single?’","He stared at himself with a complicated expression.","’Even after all this time, not a single woman has fallen for me.’","He sighed. \"Well, whatever.\"","As he turned away from the mirror, something else caught his attention. Floating in the air before him was a familiar translucent window.","The System. And it was currently waiting to reward him.","Noah’s eyes immediately lit up. He had been extremely curious about what his reward would be.","After all, this time he had faced a Monarch.","Even though the Monarch of Decay had not appeared in its true form, Noah had still fought against one of the most terrifying existences in the world—and survived.","Not only that... He had even contributed to its defeat.","That alone was an achievement far beyond anything he had experienced before.","’I really want to see what I got.’","His finger almost reached toward the floating notification.","But he stopped.","’Akari or someone else might come back soon. My own family might even show up.’","Noah rubbed his chin thoughtfully.","’And if this new reward turns out to be something troublesome...’","He imagined another ridiculous ability or dangerous thing appearing before him.","’That would be too much work.’","He shuddered at the thought.","’I’ll check it after everything settles down.’","He decided it was better to deal with the people around him first.","His thoughts drifted toward the Moon Goddess—the one who had helped him before. Without her intervention, he wouldn’t have survived.","’She already knew this would happen...’","A troubling thought surfaced in his mind.","’Does that mean she’s behind all of this? Or perhaps someone connected to her is?’","Noah sighed inwardly.","’I can’t tell what she’s really planning.’","As if that wasn’t enough, he had already agreed to do something for her in the future, whatever that request might be.","Noah had no idea what was truly happening around him.","’If I want to understand any of this, I need to learn more about her. Her origins, her history, her powers... anything I can find.’","He narrowed his eyes.","’The more information I have about the Moon Goddess the better chance I might have to deal with her.’","Tap.","Tap.","Just then, the sound of footsteps came from outside the chamber.","Noah immediately turned toward the door.","The footsteps grew closer to his chamber.","Slide. The door opened.","\"Noah!\" A voice came from doorstep.","A familiar woman stood in the doorway.","She was wearing a beautiful purple kimono. Her long black hair, which was usually tied into a neat bun, was now completely loose, cascading down her back like a dark waterfall.","But Noah barely noticed her hair. His attention immediately fell upon her face. Parts of her flesh were still visibly rotten.","The skin along her cheek had blackened, rotten patches spreading across it. Some areas looked as though the flesh itself had melted, leaving behind an unsettling mark of the corruption she had suffered.","Despite that, Noah recognized her instantly, how could he not?","\"Akari?\"","Before he could say anything else, she vanished from the doorway. In the blink of an eye, she appeared in front of him and wrapped her arms tightly around his body.","\"Oh, Noah!\"","Her voice trembled slightly.","\"You are finally awake. I was so scared... I was terrified of what might have happened to you.\"","Noah’s expression softened. He immediately returned the embrace, gently wrapping his arms around her.","He buried his face against the crook of her neck, feeling the warmth of her body.","\"I’m perfectly fine.\"","After a moment, he slowly pulled away. His eyes immediately fell upon her damaged face.","His expression became serious. He reached out and gently touched the corrupted skin on her cheek.","\"You... you still have... \"","\"Don’t worry about it.\"","Akari smiled calmly.","\"I’m slowly recovering.\"","She lightly touched the damaged side of her face.","\"As a dragon, my regenerative abilities are naturally much stronger than those of humans. Even this corruption can gradually be healed. It may take some time, but I’ll recover eventually.\"","She paused before adding with a faint smile, \"That’s one of the quirks of being a dragon.\"","Noah finally felt the tension leave his body. \"Thank God...\"","He let out a relieved breath. \"That means you’re safe. And eventually, you’ll return to normal.\"","Akari looked at him for a moment. Then her expression became strangely serious.","\"Why?\"","Noah blinked.","\"Why what?\"","\"Were you worried that I would remain ugly like this?\"","She tilted her head slightly. \"That I wouldn’t return to my original appearance?\"","Noah’s eyes widened.","\"NO!\"","He immediately shook his head. \"What do you mean?! It doesn’t matter at all!\"","Akari raised an eyebrow. \"I was worried about your health, that’s all. As for your appearance...\"","Noah gently touched her cheek again. \"You’re still beautiful.\" He smiled. \"And you’re still my lovely Akari.\"","For a moment, Akari’s usually cold expression remained frozen. She looked at him.","\"Hehe...\" A soft chuckle escaped her lips. Her cold demeanor finally broke. \"Noah, I’m just teasing you.\"","She smiled warmly. \"Don’t worry.\"","Noah let out a long sigh. \"Don’t scare me like that...\"","He looked at her again, relieved to see her smiling. Then he remembered something. \"Did you meet Ophelia?\"","Akari’s expression immediately softened.","She nodded. \"Yes... I did.\"","Her voice became quieter. \"I... I can’t tell you just how happy I was.\"","She lowered her gaze slightly.","\"I...\"","She seemed unable to find the right words.","Noah didn’t press her. Instead, he simply smiled and pulled her into another gentle embrace. His hand moved slowly through her long black hair, caressing it softly.","\"Well, I’m happy to be back too.\"","Akari remained quietly in his arms. After a few moments, she spoke. \"I haven’t talked to her about you yet.\"","Noah raised an eyebrow. \"I’ll scold her properly later.\"","A faint mischievous glint appeared in her eyes. \"You should come with me.\"","Noah chuckled. \"Sure.\"","Then he suddenly smiled. \"But I have an idea that might make her feel even worse.\"","Akari looked at him suspiciously. \"A small revenge isn’t a bad idea.\"","She narrowed her eyes. \"Just don’t be too cruel.\"","\"Hehe.\"","Noah placed a hand against his chest with an exaggeratedly proud expression. \"What are you talking about? I’m the kindest man in the world.\"","Akari stared at him silently.","\"...\"","Noah smiled innocently. \"So don’t worry.\"","After a brief pause, he looked at her curiously. \"Rather... did you meet your husband?\"","Akari’s expression changed slightly.","\"Hmm.\"","She nodded.","\"Yes. I did.\"","Noah’s curiosity immediately increased.","\"And?\"","He leaned slightly closer.","\"What was his reaction?\"","He asked with genuine curiosity.","Akari looked at him.","\"Well, he was genuinely shocked. He asked me what had happened and how I ended up like this...\"","\"Was he happy to see you?\" Noah asked, his curiosity growing.","Akari simply shrugged.\"No. As I told you before, we never loved each other.\"","Her expression remained calm. \"He felt nothing when he saw me again. And honestly, I didn’t feel particularly happy or angry toward him either. After sixty years, there was simply... nothing left between us for me.\"","Noah nodded slowly.","\"Ohh...\"","He paused for a moment.","\"So, what happens next?\"","A faint smile appeared on Akari’s face. \"I contacted my father. He’ll be coming here tomorrow.\"","She glanced toward the window. \"The same goes for your parents. They should be arriving soon as well.\"","Noah’s eyes widened slightly. \"Really?\"","Akari nodded. \"Most likely, I’ll return to the Eastern Duchy with my father and go back to his home.\"","Noah’s eyes immediately lit up. ’So she’s really ending her relationship with Lionel Thornveil...’","He desperately wanted to grin from ear to ear. He even had the sudden urge to hug Akari in celebration.","But he quickly restrained himself. ’Calm down, Noah. Don’t make it obvious.’ He calm himself down.","He cleared his throat and forced himself to maintain a composed expression. \"That’s great news.\"","His voice sounded far more cheerful than he intended. \"I can’t wait to see my family again.\"","He paused before adding excitedly, \"And I finally get to meet Duke Reiji Narukami!\"","Akari chuckled softly. \"Hehe. I’m looking forward to seeing my father again too.\"","The two remained silent for a moment.","Then Noah’s expression suddenly changed. A mischievous smile slowly appeared on his face.","\"Akari.\"","\"Hmm?\"","\"I have a request regarding Ophelia.\"","Akari looked at him suspiciously.","\"A request?\"","She tilted her head.","\"What kind of request?\"","Noah’s smile widened. \"Can you hear me out first?\"","For some reason Akari had guess that this request was going to be ridiculous."]},{"number":306,"title":"Chapter 306: New rewards","paragraphs":["\"Alright... no one is here. Good.\"","Noah finally found himself alone. Amusingly, no one from the Thornveil family had come to see him yet.","It surprised him a little, but honestly, he didn’t care.","Akari had wanted to stay with him for a little longer, but Noah had insisted that she spend the day with her daughter.","After being separated for sixty years, at least sixty years for Akari, while twelve years for Ophelia, they undoubtedly had a lot to talk about.","’What was their first meeting like?’","Noah couldn’t help but wonder.","’Did they cry when they saw each other? Did they spend hours talking?’","He smiled faintly.","He could only imagine what their reunion must have been like.","For the past few months, Noah had grown accustomed to sleeping beside Akari. Having her presence next to him had gradually become something he took for granted.","But now he turned his head toward the empty side of the bed.","There was no one there.","’It feels a little empty.’","If Akari were beside him right now, he would probably have already pulled her into his arms and cuddled with her.","Noah sighed. \"Whatever.\"","He shook his head and looked toward the empty air in front of him.","\"I should check what reward I got this time.\"","A hint of excitement appeared in his eyes.","\"I hope it’s something awesome.\"","He had been holding back his curiosity for long enough. He couldn’t wait any longer and decided to check it.","There was no reason to wait anymore.","[A Reward Is Available.]","[Would you like to claim it?]","[ YES ]","Noah stared at the notification for several seconds.","Then he slowly raised his hand.","His movements were still sluggish from exhaustion, but he managed to extend his finger toward the floating button.","Tap.","His fingertip touched [YES].","The translucent screen instantly dissolved into countless particles of light before reforming in front of him.","A mechanical voice echoed directly inside his mind.","[Congratulations, Extra!]","[You have successfully survived the First Act of Chapter II — \"Glimpse of Decay.\"]","Noah’s eyes narrowed slightly.","The notification continued.","[Despite encountering numerous dangers within the Labyrinth, you have successfully survived the battle.]","[You eliminated every obstacle in Labyrinth, entered the realm created by the Dragon of Chaos, assisted in the awakening of the Storm Dragon’s bloodline, confronted the Monarch of Decay, protected the newly awakened Storm Dragon, and successfully returned to the real world.]","[For your courage and extraordinary achievements, two rewards have been granted.]","Noah’s eyes immediately brightened.","’Two rewards?’","The excitement in his heart grew.","Then the next notification appeared.","[Rewards Granted:]","[Active Ability Acquired — Puppet of the Frost Dragon.]","[Special Information Acquired — Map to a Mythical-Rank Weapon.]","Noah blinked.","\"Puppet of the Frost Dragon?\"","He immediately focused on the ability. The moment he did, information flooded into his mind.","It wasn’t merely a name.","He instinctively understood how the ability worked.","Puppet of the Frost Dragon allowed its user to gather their mana and condense it into the form of a massive dragon made entirely from ice and frost.","The resulting Frost Dragon would obey Noah’s commands and could be controlled freely by him.","Its strength, however, depended on the user’s own power. The stronger the user became, the larger and more powerful the Frost Dragon could be.","At Noah’s current level, he could only create a relatively small Frost Dragon.","But as his strength continued to increase... The creature’s size could grow from several meters. To dozens of meters.","And eventually, perhaps even more meters. There was only one major limitation.","Mana consumption.","The larger and more powerful the Frost Dragon was, the greater the amount of mana required to create and maintain it.","Noah’s eyes sparkled.","’So it’s basically an ice dragon that I can create and control.’","A grin slowly spread across his face.","’Not bad. Guess it was for helping a dragon.’","Then his attention shifted toward the second reward.","[Map to a Mythical-Rank Weapon.]","Noah expected an actual map to appear. Perhaps an ancient parchment. Maybe even a mysterious treasure map.","But nothing appeared in his hands.","Instead a strange sensation suddenly spread through his mind.","\"Eh?\"","Noah froze. Information began pouring directly into his consciousness.","He saw a location. A vast snowy mountain range covered in constant ice blizzard.","An enormous mountain. A particular valley hidden deep within the mountains.","He could visualize the surrounding terrain, the route leading toward it, and even the approximate position of the weapon.","It was as though someone had carved the entire location directly into his memory.","Noah’s eyes widened.","’So... I don’t actually get a physical map.’","The System had instead implanted the information directly into his mind.","He knew where the weapon was. He knew the general route to reach it. He even knew the landmarks surrounding its location.","The information was so clear that he couldn’t possibly forget it.","Noah remained silent for several seconds. Then a grin slowly appeared on his face.","’A Mythical-rank weapon...’","His excitement was impossible to hide. He leaned back against the bed.","\"This reward...\"","He couldn’t help but smile.","\"Is actually pretty damn good.\"","But then his smile vanished.","\"But the place... The Northern Continent, Glaciara... This isn’t going to be easy. Fuck!!\"","The system window disappeared from before him.","Noah sighed.","The rewards had been given, and they were great... yet, at the same time, not particularly useful. At least, not for now.","The dragon would certainly be useful, but its true potential would only shine once Noah reached the peak of his current rank.","The weapon, however, was perfect for him. A Mythical-rank weapon—something that could potentially cut through the skin of Sovereign-level humans with ease, even without channeling mana into it.","At least, that was what Noah expected from it.","\"But what could that weapon be...?\"","He thought for a moment before shrugging.","\"Well, it doesn’t matter. With my Combatant profession, I can use any weapon anyway.\"","Noah exhaled in relief and closed his eyes.","For now, there was nothing more he could do.","It was time to sleep without a single worry on his mind."]},{"number":307,"title":"Chapter 307: Reunion [1]","paragraphs":["A few hours earlier, while Noah was still unconscious...","Thornveil Estate.","It was morning, yet the entire estate was filled with chaos and hurried footsteps. But strangely enough, it wasn’t because some powerful being had attacked them.","Nor was it because the mysterious monsters that had been pouring out of the unknown portal had suddenly returned.","Quite the opposite, it was because they had all died.","Every single one of those terrifying creatures scattered throughout the forest had suddenly collapsed and perished at almost the exact same moment.","It was an unbelievable sight. A month ago, a mysterious portal had suddenly appeared in the forest outside Everhold City.","From that portal, countless strange creatures had emerged without end.","At first, their numbers hadn’t been much of a concern.","Everhold was home to many powerful humans, including several peak-level mages and formidable warriors. Dealing with the creatures themselves had been difficult, but far from impossible.","The real problem had begun when the portal refused to close.","No matter what they tried, even the strongest mages had been unable to seal it.","For weeks, they had fought desperately to find a solution while the creatures continued pouring into the world.","Eventually, after countless attempts, they finally discovered a method to seal the portal. But by then, it was already too late.","Far too many creatures had escaped into the surrounding forest.","Even after weeks of hunting them down, only about half had been eliminated. The rest remained scattered throughout the vast wilderness, making the forest an extremely dangerous place.","And then, without warning they all died and that also the same time.","Naturally, everyone was relieved. But alongside that relief came an even stronger question.","Why? What had caused so many creatures that even strong warriors struggled to kill to suddenly perish all at once?","---","Inside Thornveil Estate, a young woman hurried through the corridor.","She wore black trousers and a neatly tucked white shirt. Her dark-blue hair was tied into a ponytail, swaying slightly behind her as she walked.","Her expression was filled with curiosity and concern. She had been trying to find someone who might know what had happened.","Instructor Morgana.","Morgana had been staying at the Thornveil Estate for the past month while searching for Noah, who had mysteriously disappeared.","The young woman had decided to speak with her. However, when she reached Morgana’s chamber and opened the door, she found it empty.","She frowned.","\"Where did she go?\"","Before she could think any further, loud voices suddenly echoed from downstairs.","\"What happened?\"","\"Everyone, hurry!\"","\"They’re here!\"","\"Open the gate!\"","The voices of servants and knights filled the manor. Footsteps thundered through the corridors as everyone rushed toward the main entrance.","The young woman blinked in surprise. Curious, she quickly followed them.","When she reached the main hall, she found nearly every servant and knight gathered around the enormous entrance doors.","She squeezed through the crowd and stepped outside. Her eyes immediately fell upon two familiar figures.","Her father stood near the entrance.","Lionel Thornveil.","The Duke stood tall and imposing, his dark-blue hair neatly combed and his emerald eyes fixed toward the estate gates.","Beside him stood his now wife, Sofia. The woman wore an elegant gown, her light-brown hair falling gracefully around her shoulders.","The young woman was about to approach them and ask what was happening when something beyond the gates caught her attention.","Two figures were walking toward the estate.","The first was someone she knew, Morgana. The instructor was walking slowly, carrying someone in her arms.","The moment the young woman recognized the person in Morgana’s arms, her eyes widened. It was Noah.","His clothes were completely tattered, his body covered in dirt and injuries. His eyes were closed. He was unconscious.","’He was found?’ She thought.","But then her gaze shifted. There was another person walking beside Morgana.","A woman, she was wearing a kimono that had been torn and damaged in several places.","Her black hair was tied into a messy bun, and her face was partially covered with ugly, blackened patches of damaged flesh around her cheek and neck. She looked unknown to her, at first glance.","Yet those blue eyes. Those familiar blue eyes.","Ophelia’s breath caught in her throat. Her heart suddenly began pounding against her chest.","She knew her. She didn’t need anyone to tell her who that woman was. She had spent countless nights wondering what it would be like if her mother was alive.","Countless years imagining what it would feel like to see her again.","And now she was standing right there.","Her mother Akari.","Ophelia took a hesitant step forward, then another.","Her legs trembled beneath her. For a moment, she couldn’t move. She couldn’t breathe properly. Her mind seemed to go completely blank.","Was this real? Was she really standing there? After all these years?","Akari had also noticed her.","She suddenly stopped walking. Their eyes met. Those familiar blue eyes widened in disbelief.","Neither of them moved. Then Akari’s expression slowly changed. The shock in her eyes softened.","Her lips trembled. Tears began gathering in the corners of her eyes.","\"Lia...\"","Her voice was barely more than a whisper. But to Ophelia it was loud enough to shatter every wall she had built around her heart.","Lia, that was what her mother used to call her, no one else but only her. The moment she heard that name, the emotions she had kept buried for years finally broke free.","Tears immediately filled Ophelia’s eyes. She tried to speak. She wanted to say something.","’Mother.’","But no words came out. Her throat tightened. Her vision blurred. And then before she knew she ran.","\"Mother!\"","She rushed forward and threw herself into Akari’s arms.","Akari barely had time to react before Ophelia wrapped both arms tightly around her.","The moment their bodies touched, Ophelia broke down. She buried her face against her mother’s chest and began crying uncontrollably.","Her shoulders trembled. Years of loneliness, longing, confusion, sadness of her death.","She had imagined this moment so many times. Even though she knew it was impossible. Sometimes, she had imagined herself angrily asking god why her mother have to die so early.","But now that it was actually happening. She couldn’t say any of those things. She didn’t care about the questions. How could she still alive? She didn’t care about that right now.","She only wanted to hold her. To make sure she was real. To make sure she wouldn’t disappear again.","\"Mother...\"","Her voice cracked.","\"I... I thought I’d never see you again...\"","Akari’s eyes trembled.","She slowly wrapped her arms around her daughter. The moment she felt Ophelia’s warmth, something inside her broke.","She had imagined this reunion countless times during the sixty years she had been trapped. She had wondered how Ophelia had grown.","Whether she was happy. Whether she was enjoying her life. Whether she had forgotten her. And now her daughter was standing in her arms, crying like a little child.","Akari’s tears finally began falling. She gently buried one hand into Ophelia’s hair and held her tightly.","\"I’m sorry...\"","Her voice trembled.","\"I’m so sorry, Lia.\"","Ophelia shook her head violently against her chest.","\"Don’t...\"","She tightened her arms around Akari.","\"Don’t apologize...\"","Her tears continued to fall.","\"I just...\"","She struggled to breathe between her sobs.","\"I just wanted you... I thought... you died... but now you are here mom.\"","Akari closed her eyes. Hearing those words hurt more than any wound she had suffered. She held her daughter even tighter.","\"I’m here now.\"","Her voice was soft and trembling.","\"I’m here, Lia.\"","After a long sixty years. Akari could finally hold her daughter again. Ophelia could finally feel what it was like to be held by her mother once again.","---","[A/N: Don’t curse me as why i wrote this Chapter!! I just wanted to give you rough summary about what happened in city while Noah was inside, how much time pass, and short reunion. Hm.. it’s definitely not because i was confused for what to write further. Yup definitely not!! Now don’t look at me with suspicious gaze!!]"]},{"number":308,"title":"Chapter 308: Reunion [2]","paragraphs":["Next day.","\"Noah!\"","The moment he stepped into the sitting room, a woman with wheat-blonde hair and beautiful blue eyes rushed toward him.","Before Noah could even react, she threw her arms around him and hugged him tightly.","\"Mother...\"","Noah smiled softly and wrapped his arms around her.","This was his mother, Catelyn Eldritch.","For the past month, she had been forced to endure the uncertainty of not knowing where her son was or whether he was even alive. Now that he was finally standing in front of her, she seemed unable to hold back her emotions.","\"Where have you been?\" she whispered, her voice trembling. \"I was so worried about you!\"","She rested her face against his shoulder as tears slowly streamed down her cheeks.","Noah’s expression softened.","\"Mother, it’s all right. I’m here now. I’m fine and safe.\"","He gently patted her back, trying to reassure her. But even as he comforted her, he could feel her body trembling slightly in his arms.","That trembling alone told him just how much she had worried about him.","How much she loved him. And how terrified she must have been during the days when there had been no news of him.","A warm feeling slowly spread through Noah’s chest.","Beside them stood a man with silver-white hair and violet eyes. He appeared to be in his thirties, though his calm and dignified presence made him seem older.","He was Noah’s father, Julian Eldritch.","His expression was normally composed, but even he couldn’t completely hide the relief in his eyes. Not far from him stood another young man with wheat-blonde hair and violet eyes.","His older brother, Nathan Eldritch, wore a wide smile as he watched the reunion.","They were currently inside one of the sitting rooms of the Thornveil Estate.","Noah’s family had arrived that morning the moment they learned that he had finally been found. And the instant Noah had stepped through the door, his mother had rushed to him.","Looking at her now, Noah couldn’t help but feel something stir deep within his heart.","’It has only been a little over a month since I disappeared in this world... But they look as though they haven’t seen me in years.’","His gaze moved from his mother to his father and then to Nathan. Despite everything that had happened to him, this moment felt strangely peaceful.","’So this is what it feels like to come home.’","For the first time since arriving in this world, Noah truly understood the meaning of familiar love. The kind of warmth that didn’t require words.","The kind of love that simply existed because they were family. Eventually, Catelyn slowly released him.","She wiped the tears from her cheeks, though her eyes were still slightly red.","Julian stepped forward. First, he simply looked into his son’s eyes. Then he raised a hand and gently patted Noah’s shoulder.","\"It’s good to see you safe and back.\"","His voice was calm, but the relief behind those words was unmistakable. Then he narrowed his eyes slightly.","\"And I can tell you’ve grown stronger in such a short time.\"","Noah smiled. \"I had quite the adventure.\"","Before Julian could respond, Nathan suddenly stepped forward and pulled Noah into a tight hug.","\"I’m so glad you’re back, little brother!\"","\"Argh!\"","Noah’s face immediately twisted in discomfort. \"Oi! Don’t use your physical strength!\"","\"Oh!\"","Nathan quickly realized what he was doing and released him.","\"Haha! Sorry!\"","He rubbed the back of his head sheepishly. \"I was just too happy and relieved.\"","Noah shook his head with a helpless smile. \"You haven’t changed at all.\"","\"Of course not.\"","Nathan grinned. \"Someone has to make sure you don’t get too serious.\"","Catelyn couldn’t help but smile at the sight of her two sons.","Even Julian’s usually stern expression softened. The room was filled with nothing but the warmth of family.","Noah looked at them quietly. He had experienced countless dangerous moments before coming back home.","And now standing here with his family felt more comforting than any victory.","He had finally returned home.","Then, just as the peaceful atmosphere settled over the room, another voice suddenly broke the silence.","\"So... you are Noah Eldritch.\"","Noah’s smile faded slightly. He turned toward the source of the voice.","Someone else was in the sitting room.","And from the tone of that voice alone, Noah could tell that this reunion was far from over.","Several figures were already seated on the sofas.","Lionel Thornveil sat beside his wife, Sofia, while Ophelia, the woman who had once been Noah’s fiancée sat quietly beside them.","Across from them sat two people. One of them was someone Noah knew all too well.","Akari, She was dressed in a clean, beautiful kimono, looking far more presentable than when Noah had last seen her.","Her long black hair had been neatly tied into a traditional bun, and although the corruption still remained on parts of her face and neck, her condition had clearly improved.","Beside her sat the other man. The same man who had just called out to Noah.","A stranger, at least, a stranger to Noah’s eyes.","The man slowly rose from his seat.","He was tall easily over six feet with a broad, imposing build. He wore a simple black yukata, and his black hair was neatly tied behind his head. Judging by his appearance, he seemed to be in his early fifties.","His presence alone carried a natural dignity. Even without anyone introducing him, Noah already knew exactly who he was.","He had never met the man face-to-face before, but he had heard enough about him.","Reiji Narukami.","The Duke of the Eastern Duchy of Raigamine.","Akari’s father.","Noah’s eyes briefly met the older man’s gaze.","Reiji’s blue eyes studied him quietly.","Noah couldn’t help but feel a faint sense of pressure from the man’s presence.","’So this is Akari’s father... I need to have a good first impression.’","He had been curious about the man ever since Akari told him that her father would be coming to see her.","And now, standing before him, Duke Reiji Narukami looked every bit like someone who had ruled one of the most powerful duchies in the empire for decades."]},{"number":309,"title":"Chapter 309: Reiji Narukami","paragraphs":["Noah continued looking at the man for a moment before straightening his posture and giving him a respectful bow.","\"It’s an honor to meet you, Lord Narukami.\"","Reiji said nothing. He simply walked toward Noah.","Noah remained bowed for a few seconds before finally straightening.","Standing at around six feet one himself, Noah had grown slightly taller after his battle with the Monarch of Decay.","Yet despite his height, Reiji still seemed far more intimidating.","The Duke stood well over six feet tall, and when he stopped in front of Noah, his imposing figure made Noah feel as though he were being looked down upon.","Then, unexpectedly, a smile appeared on Reiji’s face.","\"Come here, young man.\"","Before Noah could react, Reiji raised his hand and gave him a firm pat on the shoulder just like Julian did.","THUD!","\"Argh!\"","Noah’s knees nearly buckled from the sheer force.","’What the hell?!’","He quickly steadied himself. He absolutely refused to show weakness in front of Akari’s father.","Reiji burst into loud laughter. \"Hahaha! Young man, Noah! I’ve heard quite a lot about you from my daughter.\"","His violet eyes gleamed with amusement as he looked Noah up and down.","\"But seeing you in person is something else entirely. You’re already at the high stage of the Condensed Core at your age.\"","He shook his head in disbelief.","\"Remarkable. Truly remarkable.\"","Noah gave a modest smile and nodded.","\"Thank you for the compliment, Lord Narukami. But I believe I’m still far from being good enough.\"","Reiji’s eyes widened for a moment.","\"HAHAHAHA!\"","His laughter filled the room. \"I like that!\" He gave Noah another heavy pat on the shoulder.","Noah’s body stiffened.","\"Someone who refuses to be satisfied with his progress despite already accomplishing so much.\"","Reiji grinned.","\"Good! Very good!\"","His gaze shifted toward Julian.","\"Your son is an impressive young man. He isn’t the same Noah everyone used to know.\"","Julian smiled faintly. \"Yes. It’s true. My son has changed considerably.\"","His expression softened as he looked at Noah. \"And as his father, I’m happy and proud to see it.\"","Reiji nodded. \"Indeed.\"","He leaned back slightly, his expression becoming more solemn. \"Well, let’s forget about all those old matters.\"","His eyes moved toward Akari. \"My daughter has returned.\"","There was a faint tremble in his voice as he spoke those words. \"Knowing that she is alive...\"","He paused. \"That alone is the greatest gift and happiness I have received in the past twelve years.\"","Akari lowered her eyes slightly. A faint smile appeared on her lips. Noah noticed the slight redness around her eyes.","’She cried...’ He didn’t need to ask. ’It must have been after meeting her father.’","Seeing Akari like that made Noah smile quietly. Reiji clapped his hands together.","\"Now, why is everyone still standing? Come, sit down.\"","Everyone moved toward the sofas.","The room had been specifically designed for gatherings, family meetings, and entertaining important guests. It was spacious enough for everyone to sit comfortably without feeling crowded.","Julian, Catelyn, and Nathan sat together on one sofa. Noah sat beside Akari. He glanced at her again. Her eyes were still slightly red, but there was unmistakable happiness in them.","It was the expression of someone who had finally found something precious that she thought she had lost forever.","Before anyone could say much else, Reiji suddenly spoke. \"We should have a celebration tonight.\"","Everyone looked toward him. \"Not only have my daughter and Noah returned safely, but those mysterious monsters have also been eliminated, and those troublesome portals finally disappeared.\"","\"Cough! Cough!\"","Lionel cleared his throat awkwardly.","\"This is my house, father.\"","Silence. Reiji slowly turned his head toward him. His blue eyes narrowed.","\"Lionel.\"","Lionel’s expression immediately became stiff. \"Don’t call me father or father-in-law.\"","Reiji’s tone was calm, but there was unmistakable authority behind it. \"We already discussed this yesterday. My daughter will be returning with me.\"","His gaze shifted toward Akari. \"And she is no longer your wife.\"","Lionel remained silent. Reiji’s eyes then moved toward Sofia. The woman flinched slightly under his cold gaze.","\"You have already married someone else.\"","His voice remained firm. \"So I hope you don’t intend to continue calling my daughter your wife.\"","Lionel remained quiet for several seconds. Eventually, he sighed. \"Yes. You’re right. We already discussed this yesterday over the phone.\"","He lowered his gaze slightly. \"Sorry, Lord Reiji.\"","Reiji simply nodded and looked away.","Meanwhile, Ophelia sat quietly on the sofa. Unlike everyone else, she seemed unusually nervous.","Her mother had finally returned. After twelve years, she had finally been reunited with Akari, who everyone thought was dead.","But now a question kept weighing heavily on her mind.","’What happens now?’","There was time when she had such deep hatred for demons. There were few demons who ran away that day, and she wanted to find them and kill them. She wanted power, she wanted to be duchess.","But her mother was back, now there was no reason for revenge.","Would her mother leave with her grandfather? Would she stay here? And if Akari returned to the Eastern Duchy.","’What about me?’","Would her father allow her to go with her? Ophelia nervously glanced toward Akari.","She wanted to ask. But she was afraid of the answer. She had only just gotten her mother back. She didn’t want to lose her again.","And then there’s Noah, he seemed to be very close with her mother and same goes for her. Unknown discomfort started to form inside Ophelia.","Meanwhile, Noah’s attention was focused on something entirely different.","’Did Akari tell everyone what happened in that place?’","He hadn’t asked her what she had told Lionel or Duke Reiji.","Yet neither of them had mentioned anything about the mysterious realm, the ancient dragon trapping, or the Monarch of Decay.","Even his own parents hadn’t brought it up.","’That means she either handled the matter herself...’","Noah’s eyes narrowed slightly. ’Or they’re deliberately avoiding the topic.’","There were several possibilities. Perhaps Akari had already explained everything privately to her father and Lionel.","Or perhaps they simply didn’t want to discuss something so dangerous in front of the younger generation.","After all, whatever had happened inside that realm involved beings far beyond anything ordinary people could comprehend.","Noah leaned back slightly.","’Whatever the reason is... I doubt this is something they want to talk about openly when they are with family. I will ask Akari later.’","For now, he decided not to ask. If Akari wanted him to know what she had told them, she would tell him herself.","And judging from the expressions of the adults in the room."]},{"number":310,"title":"Chapter 310: Talking with Akari","paragraphs":["Eventually, the conversation came to an end. Noah wanted to speak with Akari alone. The problem was when would he get the chance?","After the gathering, it was decided that Noah’s family would stay at the Thornveil Estate for the night.","Fortunately, the Eldritch Duchy and its main city, where Noah’s family lived, had not suffered any attacks from the mysterious monsters.","Because of that, Julian wasn’t in any particular hurry to return. He had left the city in the hands of his trusted knights for the time being.","After some time, Noah finally managed to slip away from the others.","He wanted to find Akari.","\"Where is she? I want to talk to her.\"","He walked through the beautiful corridors of the Thornveil Estate, occasionally glancing at the expensive decorations and paintings hanging along the walls.","The manor was enormous, with countless rooms and chambers spread throughout it.","Noah eventually stopped one of the servants and asked about Akari’s whereabouts.","After receiving directions, he continued on his way.","However, before he could reach his destination, he suddenly saw someone walking toward him from the other end of the corridor.","It was Akari.","The moment her eyes landed on him, her usually cold and strict gaze immediately softened and brightened.","She quickened her pace.","\"Noah... I was looking for you.\"","Noah nodded with a gentle smile.","\"Well, I was looking for you too. I wanted to talk to you about something important.\"","Akari nodded.","\"Then follow me.\"","She turned around and led him toward another chamber.","The manor was so large that there were plenty of unused rooms, and this particular chamber was completely empty.","Once they entered, Akari walked toward the bed and sat down.","Then she patted the empty space beside her.","Noah followed her and sat down.","\"Did you want to talk to me about something?\" Akari asked. \"What is it?\"","Noah nodded.","\"I wanted to ask you about something. What did you tell the others? Duke Lionel and your father?\"","He paused for a moment before continuing.","\"About what happened to you... who took you there... and what we faced?\"","Akari let out a quiet sigh.","\"I didn’t tell them the full truth.\"","Noah listened carefully.","\"After I returned, I first spoke with Lionel. I told him that I had been mysteriously pulled into that realm by an unknown existence twelve years ago during fight with demon. I told him that it was because I possessed a dragon bloodline and that the existence wanted me to awaken it completely.\"","Noah was slightly surprised that she revealed about her dragon bloodline.","She paused briefly.","\"Once I was there, I trained for years and eventually reached the peak of my strength. Then, one day, you appeared there.\"","Her expression became slightly more serious.","\"After that, an unknown being suddenly appeared and tried to kill us. We fought it, defeated it, and eventually found a way to return to this world.\"","Noah thought about it for a moment.","\"And he believed you?\"","\"Well... I don’t know.\"","Akari shrugged slightly.","\"But he didn’t question me any further. Besides, I didn’t exactly lie to him.\"","Noah narrowed his eyes slightly.","\"But you did hide few things, didn’t you?\"","\"Yes.\"","Akari didn’t deny it.","\"I know that I shouldn’t reveal everything about my dragon bloodline. Especially the fact that I’m now a full dragon rather than a human. But I think it was necessary to reveal.\"","Noah’s expression became serious.","\"Are you sure about that? You told him about your bloodline\"","Akari nodded.","\"Since dragons no longer exist, most people believe they were nothing more than creatures from ancient stories and legends.\"","She looked down at her hands for a moment.","\"If word gets out that I have become a dragon, I can’t even imagine the chaos it would cause throughout the world.\"","Noah remained silent.","He knew she was right.","The existence of a living dragon would undoubtedly attract countless powerful individuals, organizations, and nations.","However, Akari soon continued.","\"Lionel and my father already know that I’m a full dragon now.\"","Noah’s eyes became serious.","\"Isn’t that dangerous?\"","\"Yes, it is.\"","Akari answered honestly.","\"But I thought it was better to tell them.\"","She looked at Noah.","\"Even though I don’t love Lionel, I know he’s not a bad person, nor is he someone who is obsessed with power. I can trust him with this matter. And what happened there was something I shouldn’t hide. Also what made them more worried was the being we fought.\"","She paused before continuing.","\"Also as you know, my father’s duchy is considerably stronger than Lionel’s.\"","Her voice carried a hint of confidence.","\"We have greater strength, and now, without a doubt, I’m stronger than both Lionel and my father.\"","Noah raised an eyebrow.","\"Really?\"","\"Yes.\"","Akari nodded.","\"It seems that my strength increased after I returned to this world.\"","She glanced at her hand.","\"And it’s still growing.\"","She slowly exhaled.","\"Whatever happened inside that realm seems to have changed me in more ways than I expected.\"","Noah remained thoughtful for a moment before asking,","\"But you’re a dragon now, and Lionel knows that. Why didn’t he try to stop you from leaving?\"","His expression became slightly concerned.","\"I mean, what person wouldn’t want a dragon in their family... or even under their control?\"","Akari gave him a knowing look.","\"Well he don’t want to go against whole eastern duchy, nor me. So don’t worry. I’m strong enough to protect myself. Besides, I don’t think I can hide my identity from the world forever.\"","She glanced toward the window, her expression becoming slightly more serious.","\"Things are becoming dangerous. We have much bigger problems to worry about.\"","\"What kind of problems?\"","\"I don’t know.\"","Akari shook her head.","\"This is what my father told me. I still don’t know what’s happening in the world right now.\"","\"True. You were stuck for years.\"","Noah fell silent for a moment, thinking about everything she had said.","Then Akari suddenly gave him a soft smile.","\"Also, don’t worry.\"","She looked directly into his eyes.","\"I didn’t tell them everything you did in that place.\"","Noah immediately let out a quiet sigh of relief.","\"Thank you.\"","\"Hehe. I won’t put you in danger.\"","Akari’s expression then became curious.","\"Now, can you tell me where you got those divine powers? And do you know what that being was?\"","Noah nodded.","\"...I received those powers from the Moon Goddess. Temporarily.\"","Akari’s eyes widened.","\"The Moon Goddess?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"Why?\"","Her surprise was obvious.","\"Why would she give you her powers?\"","\"Listen...\""]},{"number":311,"title":"Chapter 311: Call her here","paragraphs":["Noah began explaining everything that had happened.","He told her about the moment he had nearly died, how he had called out for help, how he found himself on moon, and then Goddess’s voice came to him, and how she had given him her divine power.","He trusted Akari enough to tell her the truth.","After all, she was the one person who had fought alongside him through that entire nightmare. How she put her life on line to save him. She had been with him for last six month. She took care of him.","When Noah finally finished explaining everything, Akari fell silent.","She lowered her gaze, processing his words.","\"As we expected...\" Her expression became grim. \"That thing really was a Monarch. After telling Lionel and father, they also came to this conclusion. Now it’s confirmed, that thing was monarch.\"","Noah nodded.","\"And the Moon Goddess helped you because she wants you to do something for her?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"But she didn’t tell you what it is?\" She asked.","\"No. She said she’d tell me when the time comes.\"","Akari remained silent for several seconds.","\"They might comeback again.\"","Noah looked at her. \"You mean the Monarchs?\"","\"Yes.\"","Her expression became solemn. \"We don’t know their exact goals, but whatever they intend to do, it will undoubtedly be dangerous for our world.\"","She sighed. \"I’ll try to find whatever information I can about the Moon Goddess.\"","Noah also sighed. \"Please do. The whole situation is making me worried.\"","Akari smiled gently. Then she wrapped one arm around his shoulders.","\"Don’t worry. You’ll be fine. I know you will.\"","Noah smiled. \"Yeah. I’ve got you, a strong dragon.\"","For a brief moment, Akari’s expression changed. Guilt flickered across her face. She lowered her eyes.","’But I wasn’t able to protect him.’ She thought.","During their battle with the Monarch of Decay, it had been Noah who had ultimately protected her and defeated that thing.","She was supposed to be the stronger one. So what was the point of all her strength if she couldn’t even protect him?","Noah noticed the change in her expression. He gave her a gentle smile.","\"Hey. Don’t be sad.\"","Akari looked at him.","\"I know what you’re thinking.\"","Noah’s voice softened.","\"Neither of us was strong enough against a Monarch. If the Goddess hadn’t helped us, we’d both be dead.\"","Akari’s lips parted.","\"Yes, but... I still should have been the one—\"","Before she could finish, Noah leaned closer and gently kissed her cheek where the skin was still healing.","\"...What?\"","Akari froze. Her eyes widened in surprise.","\"No-Noah!\"","She immediately touched her cheek, her face becoming slightly flushed.","\"How many times have I told you not to do things like that without asking?\"","Noah gave her a teasing smirk.","\"Well, you were looking down and feeling sad. I needed to cheer you up.\"","\"That’s not a good way to cheer someone up.\"","Akari puffed out her cheeks and gave him a small pout.","Noah couldn’t help but smile. ’She’s adorable.’","He wanted shower her with kisses.","There was something strangely charming about seeing a mature woman like Akari act this cute.","Even with the darkened patches of decay still covering parts of her face, she was still beautiful in his eyes.","In fact, right now, she looked far too adorable for him to resist teasing her.","But Noah quickly pushed those thoughts aside.","\"Hey, Akari.\"","\"Hm?\"","\"Let’s put all of this aside for now.\"","He smiled. \"Let’s do what we planned yesterday.\"","Akari’s expression became slightly confused. Then she suddenly remembered his request, as what he wanted to do. How he wanted to punish Ophelia.","Noah continued,","\"Call your daughter, Ophelia. Bring her here.\"","Akari stared at him for a moment. Then she asked quietly, \"You really want to do this?\"","She asked once again. What he planned for Ophelia was dangerous. And she felt worried and nervous to do something like that to her own daughter.","\"Yes.\" There was no hesitation in his answer.","Akari sighed softly. But what Ophelia had done to Noah was totally wrong. And Akari also wanted to give her own daughter a punishment.","\"All right.\"","She reached into her storage ring. A moment later, a phone appeared in her hand.","Akari dialed her daughter’s number. It didn’t take long before the call was answered.","\"Mother?\"","\"Ophelia, come to this room immediately. I need to talk to you about something important.\" Akari didn’t mention that Noah was with her.","\"Something important? All right. I’ll be there.\"","After a few more words, Akari ended the call.","The moment the call ended, Noah suddenly began laughing like a villain who had just come up with an evil plan.","\"Hehehehehe...\"","Akari slowly turned her head toward him.","Noah’s grin widened.","\"This is going to be fun.\" He was really excited about this.","Akari could only sigh. She already had a bad feeling about this.","’This is going to be troublesome...’","---","Five minutes later.","Knock. Knock.","Someone knocked on the door. And both of them knew who was here.","\"Oh, she’s here,\" Noah muttered.","\"Yes, she is.\"","Akari took a slow breath before straightening her posture. Her expression immediately became cold and strict.","\"You can come inside.\"","At her words, the door slid open.","\"Mother, it’s me.\"","Ophelia stepped inside.","She was dressed in a simple blouse and trousers, paired with a sturdy pair of boots. Her dark-blue hair was tied neatly into a ponytail.","The moment she saw Akari, a soft smile naturally appeared on her face.","\"Mother—\"","But the smile disappeared almost instantly. Her eyes shifted beside, and froze. Noah was sitting right beside Akari on the bed.","Ophelia’s expression went blank. For a moment, she simply stared at him. Then she looked at her mother who had cold expression and then back to Noah.","The young man also stared back. A strange silence filled the room.","Akari remained seated between them, already regretting agreeing to Noah’s little plan. ’This is definitely going to be troublesome.’"]},{"number":312,"title":"Chapter 312: Apologize","paragraphs":["Ophelia entered the chamber, only to freeze in surprise.","She had been happy to spend time with her mother after finally being reunited with her. But at the same time, she had been avoiding one particular person.","And now, that very person was sitting beside her mother.","He was Noah Eldritch, he ex fiance.","Her mother had called her here, saying that she wanted to talk about something important. Ophelia had assumed they would be alone.","She had been wrong. Noah was sitting calmly beside Akari on the bed, his frost-blue eyes fixed on her.","They were slightly different from Akari’s clear blue eyes, but there was something strangely familiar about them.","Ophelia took a slow breath and forced herself to calm down. Then she slowly walked toward them.","Once she reached the bed, she looked at her mother.","\"Mother, you asked me to come here. What did you want to talk to me about?\"","Akari inhaled deeply.","Then she slowly exhaled. She remained silent for a while. It was almost as though she were preparing herself for what she was about to say.","Finally, after sometime, Akari stood up and faced her daughter.","\"Ophelia.\"","Her expression became cold and serious.","\"I didn’t bring up this matter earlier because I had only just returned, and I was overwhelmed with happiness after finally seeing you again.\"","She paused. \"But now, I think it’s time we address what happened between you and Noah.\"","Ophelia’s body stiffened.","Her breathing quickened slightly. She stared into her mother’s cold eyes, suddenly feeling nervous.","\"M-Mother...\"","Her voice trembled.","\"I did that because... because I didn’t want to marry Noah.\"","The memory came rushing back. She remembered that night clearly.","Noah had been extremely drunk. He had pushed her onto the bed, wearing that idiotic smile while leaning toward her.","\"I love you, Ophelia.\"","She remembered the fear and anger she had felt at that moment.","She could have easily overpowered him. Even drunk, Noah had never been physically stronger than her.","She could have simply pushed him away. Instead, she had screamed. She had made a huge scene, accusing him of trying to assault her.","And while Noah had been her fiancé at the time, that did not make what he had done acceptable.","Forcing or assaulting someone without their consent was wrong, regardless of their relationship. And in this case, the person involved was Ophelia—the daughter of a Duke.","Akari’s expression remained stern.","\"And for that reason, you decided to make such a huge scene?\"","Ophelia lowered her eyes.","\"Do you understand how much Noah suffered because of it? How much humiliation he endured? How many terrible names people called him afterward?\"","Akari’s voice carried disappointment.","\"You could have kept the matter quiet and spoken to your father if you truly hated his actions.\"","\"I... I had already told Father that I didn’t want to marry Noah.\"","Ophelia’s voice became shaky.","\"B-But... he never listened to me. He wanted the marriage because it would strengthen the relationship between our families. He and Noah’s father were close friends.\"","\"And because of that, you decided to ruin Noah’s life?\"","Akari’s voice became sharper.","\"What was so terrible about him?\"","She stared directly at her daughter.","\"He’s a good young man.\"","\"Mother...\"","Ophelia’s eyes began to redden.","\"But... I’m not some object that Father could simply hand over to another family.\"","Her voice cracked.","\"And Noah wasn’t the person you know now. Back then, he was... he was good for nothing. He had so many terrible habits. How could I—\"","\"So that makes what you did acceptable?\"","Akari interrupted. \"You could have waited.\"","Ophelia fell silent.","\"It’s not as though you were going to marry him immediately,\" Akari continued. \"The marriage would have happened after both of you graduated from the academy. Perhaps even later.\"","Ophelia lowered her head.","Her eyes slowly filled with tears. Her mother’s harsh words hurt more than she had expected.","She knew what she had done had consequences. She had seen what Noah became afterward.","She had watched him change. And deep down, she knew she could never take back what had happened.","Akari looked at her for several seconds before speaking again.","\"Have you ever tried to apologize to him?\"","Ophelia’s shoulders trembled slightly.","\"Have you ever genuinely thought about saying sorry?\"","\"But, Mother... what he did was—\"","\"I know.\"","Akari’s voice softened slightly, but her expression remained firm.","\"What he did was wrong.\"","Ophelia looked up.","\"But he apologized to you.\"","Akari continued.","\"Many times.\"","Her gaze remained fixed on her daughter.","\"He tried to apologize, and what did you do?\"","Ophelia’s lips trembled.","\"You insulted him each time.\"","Silence filled the room.","Akari’s words hung heavily between them. And for the first time, Ophelia didn’t know what to say.","Noah watched the exchange between mother and daughter before finally speaking.","\"Akari, it’s alright... It’s all in the past. There’s no need to bother with it anymore.\"","\"No need to bother?\" Akari turned toward him, her cold gaze returning. \"Noah, you were called a harasser, a good-for-nothing, a fool, a drunkard, and countless other things throughout noble society because of one mistake my daughter made.\"","\"Yes, but I was wrong too, so I forgive her.\" Noah spoke calmly, without a trace of resentment. \"And I know we weren’t suitable for each other in the first place. Besides...\"","He paused for a moment before continuing.","\"If that isn’t enough, I learned many things after being exiled from my family. I think... everything I have become today is partly because of that incident.\"","A faint smile appeared on his face.","\"So, in a way, I don’t hate that it happened.\"","\"But, Noah...\"","\"It’s alright, Akari. I really don’t hate her.\"","He looked at Akari with a gentle expression. Seeing his face, Akari’s anger gradually subsided. She closed her eyes and sighed before nodding.","\"Fine. If you’re truly okay with it...\"","She turned toward Ophelia. The moment their eyes met, Ophelia flinched again. She knew what she had done had been wrong. She understood that now.","But seeing her own mother speak so harshly to her while taking Noah’s side made something bitter rise within her chest.","Why? Why did her mother care so much about Noah? Why was she so angry with her?","Akari spoke calmly.","\"Alright, Ophelia. Apologize to Noah in front of me, and we’ll forget everything that happened in the past. Noah has no desire to remain on bad terms with you.\"","Ophelia clenched her fists.","\"Why...?\"","Akari frowned.","\"What do you mean, why? It’s because you did something wrong—\"","\"I know I did wrong! but why are you taking his side over your own daughter?\"","Ophelia stared directly into her mother’s eyes.","\"You’re showing him more care than you show me.\"","Akari didn’t react.","She simply stared back at her daughter.","\"Why, Mother...?\"","Ophelia’s voice trembled slightly.","\"I’m your daughter. I understand that what I did was wrong, but you’re treating me like I’m some kind of criminal...\"","Her eyes became red.","\"...while you’re being so kind to him.\"","A smile slowly bloomed across Noah’s face. It was almost as if he had been waiting for her to say those exact words.","\"Ophelia.\"","His voice immediately drew her attention.","Her reddened eyes shifted toward him.","\"...What? I’m talking to my mother right now, so don’t interfere.\"","Noah’s smile only grew wider. Without hesitation, he moved his right arm around Akari’s waist and pulled her closer.","\"Ah—!\"","Akari let out a small gasp. She glanced at Noah in surprise.","However, she didn’t stop him.","Noah looked directly at Ophelia.","\"You should speak more respectfully to me.\"","His grin widened. \"Your mother cares about me because she loves me.\"","He paused deliberately. \"No... that’s not quite right.\" He tightened his arm slightly around Akari.","\"We love each other.\"","Absolute silence spread the chamber.","Ophelia’s eyes widened so dramatically that it looked as though they might fall out of their sockets. Her gaze immediately dropped to Noah’s arm wrapped around her mother’s waist.","Then she looked at Akari.","Her mother who wasn’t stopping him. Not only that, Akari was looking away with a faint blush spreading across her cheeks.","The cold, intimidating expression she had worn moments ago was completely gone.","Ophelia’s mouth opened slightly.","\"...Mother?\"","Akari refused to meet her eyes in shame.","Noah, meanwhile, looked extremely pleased with himself. \"I’ll be your father in the future,\" he declared confidently. \"So you should show me some respect.\"","Ophelia’s expression froze.","Noah’s smile became even more mischievous.","\"And personally...\"","He leaned slightly toward her.","\"I’d prefer it if you called me Daddy.\"","\"...\"","Akari’s face turned even redder.","Noah ignored her completely.","\"Now, apologize to your new daddy~\"","He gave Ophelia a cheerful smile.","\"And then I’ll forgive you.\"","For several seconds, Ophelia simply stared at him.","Her mind had completely stopped functioning.","New... daddy?","She slowly turned toward her mother.","Akari was still avoiding eye contact.","That alone told Ophelia everything she needed to know.","Her expression became utterly horrified. \"No way...\"","Noah’s grin widened. \"Oh, absolutely.\""]},{"number":313,"title":"Chapter 313: Sweet Moment [1]","paragraphs":["Ophelia remained silent, completely confused and slightly terrified.","The words Noah had just spoken felt less like reality and more like something straight out of a nightmare.","She immediately looked toward her mother.","Akari was looking away, a faint blush spreading across her cheeks. She looked almost like a young maiden who had just fallen in love.","’No... this can’t be real.’","Ophelia desperately tried to convince herself otherwise. She swallowed nervously before speaking.","\"Mother... tell me this is false.\"","Her voice trembled slightly. She was clearly shaken. And if that wasn’t bad enough, Noah had actually asked her to call him Daddy.","There was absolutely no way in hell she was going to call him that. Akari, who had remained silent throughout the exchange, finally turned toward her daughter.","She seemed to understand exactly what Ophelia was going through. Yet, instead of trying to comfort her, Akari simply looked into her daughter’s reddened eyes.","\"...Yes. It is true.\"","Akari hesitated.","\"Noah and I... we...\"","She closed her eyes, seemingly embarrassed by the words she was about to say.","\"We love each other.\"","Ophelia froze.Her mother’s acceptance hit her harder than anything else could have. She took several steps backward, shaking her head in denial.","\"No...\"","Her voice was barely a whisper.","\"This can’t be...\" She shook her head harder. \"It has to be a dream... Yes, that’s it. This is just a dream. A very bad dream...\"","Her gaze fell upon Noah. He was standing beside Akari with an unbearably satisfied smile on his face.","’There’s no way my mother would fall for someone like Noah...’","Meanwhile, Noah was thoroughly enjoying himself. The reaction he was getting from Ophelia was priceless.","How many months had he spent wanting to get back at her for treating him like a criminal? And now, finally, he had the perfect opportunity.","Since she was Akari’s daughter, he had decided not to take any serious revenge against her. But this much? Surely, this was harmless.","\"Ophelia,\" Akari said.","Ophelia looked toward her mother.","\"This isn’t a dream. What you heard is the truth.\"","She paused before continuing. \"And as Noah said, you should show him respect as your new...\"","Akari’s face reddened again. She turned her head away. It took her several seconds to gather the courage to finish the sentence. \"He is your new daddy.\"","Ophelia’s eyes widened.","\"Now apologize to your daddy.\"","Those words made Ophelia clench both fists tightly. She lowered her head, staring at the floor.","\"Moth—\"","\"Ophelia!\"","Akari’s voice cut her off. \"I told you to apologize to your dad. Right now!\"","For other this might sound cringe, but not to Noah. The words dad and daddy coming from Akari’s mouth sounded like sweet music to Noah’s ears.","To Ophelia, however, they felt like arrows piercing straight through her heart.","She slowly turned toward Noah. Their eyes met.","The moment she saw him standing there, the guilt she had been trying to suppress came rushing back.","She was blind in her rage, thinking that every bad thing was happening only to her. That she was suffering, that everyone around her doesn’t care about her.","So she never care about other. She selfishly thought about her own good.","\"I... I’m sorry, Noa—\"","\"Not Noah.\"","Noah immediately corrected her.","Ophelia’s lips trembled. She nodded reluctantly. She exactly knew what he mean.","\"I-I’m sorry, D-D-Daddy...\" Even saying that word seemed to cause her physical pain. \"I apologize for what I did to you.\"","Tears began rolling down her cheeks. They were warm against her flushed skin. Her voice trembled as she began sobbing.","\"I’m sorry... I shouldn’t have done that. I was wrong... I was really wrong...\"","More tears spilled from her eyes.","\"I’ll do anything you say... just forgive me.\"","She continued crying, unable to stop the tears from flowing.","Noah and Akari watched her silently. They exchanged a glance. Then, almost simultaneously, they nodded.","Noah looked back at the crying Ophelia. He finally released his arm from around Akari’s waist and walked toward Ophelia.","When he reached her, he extended his hand and gently placed it on top of her head. He slowly stroked her hair.","A gentle smile appeared on his face. \"There, there...\" His voice was surprisingly soft. \"It wasn’t that hard to say you’re sorry, right?\"","He spoke in the same gentle tone a father might use when comforting his child.","Ophelia didn’t reject his touch. Instead, she slowly looked up at his handsome face through her tear-filled eyes.","\"Yes... I’m sorry.\"","Her voice was quiet.","\"I know what I did was wrong. I don’t deserve your forgiveness.\"","Noah smiled. \"Well, I forgive you.\"","He lightly patted her head. \"Because you were such a good girl just now.\"","Ophelia stopped sobbing for a moment. She blinked several times, her eyes still filled with tears.","\"Really...?\"","Noah nodded.","\"Of course.\"","He continued gently patting her head.","\"You were a good girl. And I hope you’ll continue being a good girl from now on.\"","Ophelia’s already reddened cheeks became even redder. She sniffled and nodded obediently.","\"Yes... I will.\"","Akari watched the scene from the side. For some reason, it genuinely looked as though a father was talking to his daughter.","Despite the fact that Noah and Ophelia were practically the same age.","It was strangely funny. But as Akari continued watching Noah gently pat and stroke Ophelia’s head, another feeling slowly began to surface within her.","It was discomfort. For some reason, she didn’t like how close Noah was standing to her daughter. She didn’t like how gently he was speaking to Ophelia. She didn’t like the soft smile on his face.","Every little thing about the scene bothered her.","Akari’s cheeks puffed up slightly. Before she even realized it, she had begun pouting.","’Why is Noah acting so close to my daughter?’","She frowned.","’She’s no longer his fiancée.’","The thought only made her more annoyed. Finally, unable to endure it any longer, Akari spoke.","\"Noah.\"","Her voice was cold, colder than she intended to be.","---","[A/N: I wrote this Chapter for fun hahaha!! Nothing much! So don’t take it seriously and enjoy it!!]"]},{"number":314,"title":"Chapter 314: Sweet Moment [2]","paragraphs":["\"Noah.\"","A cold voice broke Noah’s focus from a gentle moment. He immediately stopped stroking Ophelia’s head and turned toward the source of the voice.","Ophelia also followed his gaze, toward the familiar voice.","Akari stood a few steps away with her arms crossed beneath her chest. Her cheeks were slightly puffed out, making her look unexpectedly adorable.","But her eyes were cold, very cold.","Noah immediately sensed danger.","\"Akari... did something happen?\" he asked cautiously. \"Ophelia just apologized, so why are you angry?\"","The moment he asked that, Akari’s expression became even colder. It was as though his question had somehow made her even more irritated.","Noah’s body stiffened.","’This is new.’","He had seen Akari angry before. It wasn’t exactly unfamiliar to him. Usually, however, she became angry whenever he acted recklessly or refused to listen to her during training.","But this time? Everything had gone smoothly.","Ophelia had apologized.","Noah had forgiven her.","There shouldn’t have been anything left to be angry about. So why was Akari looking at him like that?","Ophelia, meanwhile, looked between her mother and Noah. Then back at her mother. Then at Noah. And suddenly something clicked in her mind. As if she understood what was going on.","Her eyes widened.","\"D-Dad...\"","Noah frowned.","Ophelia sighed internally.","’Why is he acting so dense? Isn’t he good at reading people?’","She quickly decided that staying here any longer was probably dangerous.","\"Well, I think I’ll take my leave for now,\" she said hurriedly. \"We can talk later. For now, you should probably figure out why Mother is angry.\"","\"Huh?\"","Noah looked confused.","\"There’s no need to call me Dad...\"","He paused. \"Not yet, at least. Also don’t tell anyone about this.\"","Ophelia stared at him for a moment. Then she nodded.","\"Okay, Noah. See you two later.\"","With that, she quickly turned on her heels and hurried out of the room. The door closed behind her. She never looked back, not even once.","Silence descended.","Noah slowly turned around.","Akari was still standing there. Her arms remained crossed, while one of her feet tapped repeatedly against the floor.","Tap.","Tap.","Tap.","She looked like someone patiently waiting for an explanation.","Noah swallowed. He had no idea what explanation this woman was expecting from him.","\"Wh-what is it, Akari?\"","Akari narrowed her eyes.","\"Hmph.\"","Noah became even more nervous.","Finally, she spoke. \"You told her not to call you Dad.\"","\"Yes...?\"","\"That means...\" Akari’s cheeks puffed up again. \"Are you still interested in my daughter?\"","Noah’s eyes widened.","\"What?!\"","\"You still want her, don’t you? You want to marry her.\" She looked away slightly, her expression filled with irritation. \"I mean... you were acting so close to her just now.\"","Noah stared at her in disbelief. \"No, no! Absolutely not!\"","He immediately shook his head. \"Why would you even think that? I was just being nice to her!\"","\"Hmph.\"","Akari turned her head away. \"You weren’t.\"","\"What?\"","\"You looked like a man trying his best to seduce a woman.\"","\"Hey! I wasn’t!\" Noah protested immediately.","Akari ignored him and continued looking away.","Noah stared at her.","She wasn’t looking at him. Her cheeks were puffed out. Her arms were crossed. Her foot was tapping impatiently against the floor.","And suddenly, a thought crossed his mind.","’Wait...’","A smile slowly spread across his face.","’Could she be jealous?’","It was probably the last thing he would have expected from Akari.","But when he thought about her behavior... It actually made perfect sense.","Noah’s smile widened. He walked toward her.","Akari noticed his approaching footsteps and glanced at him from the corner of her eye.","Noah continued walking closer, a mischievous smile playing on his lips.","\"So...\"","He stopped in front of her.","\"My Akari...\"","Akari’s eyebrow twitched. She already guess, that Noah was going to something weird.","\"...is jealous?\"","The moment those words left his mouth, Akari’s composure shattered. Her arms immediately uncrossed as she took a step backward.","\"I-I wasn’t jealous!\"","She glared at him.","\"And why would I be jealous?!\"","Noah didn’t answer. Instead, he suddenly rushed forward and wrapped his arms tightly around her.","\"Ahh!\"","Akari gasped in surprise. She could have easily avoided him. In fact, avoiding his embrace would have been effortless.","But after spending so many months with Noah, she had grown accustomed to his hugs. Somewhere along the way, she had stopped instinctively avoiding them.","And this time was no different. She simply allowed him to hold her.","Noah gently rubbed his cheek against hers. \"I’m sorry,\" he whispered. \"I didn’t mean to make you jealous. I swear.\"","\"S-shut up!\"","Akari’s voice was muffled against him.","\"And I’m not jealous!\"","Noah chuckled. He could feel her warmth against his body.","Akari was slightly taller than him by a few centimeters, despite Noah already standing over six feet tall.","It didn’t bother him in the slightest.","’I’ll surpass her height eventually.’","He was confident that with time, he would grow even taller as he rank up.","Akari remained pouting for a while, but her expression gradually softened. The irritation slowly disappeared from her face, replaced by a faint blush.","Then, almost unconsciously, her arms moved around him. She gently wrapped them around his body and held him.","Noah smiled. Then he leaned closer and planted a soft kiss on her cheek.","Akari’s body stiffened slightly. Her heartbeat quickened. And Noah’s heart wasn’t doing any better.","\"Hehe~\"","Akari’s lips curved into a small smile.","\"That’s enough, Noah. I’m not angry anymore...\"","But Noah didn’t release her. Instead, he continued holding her tightly.","\"Okay.\"","He smiled contentedly.","\"But let me stay like this for a little longer. I’m happy today.\"","Akari blinked.","\"Happy?\"","\"Yeah.\"","Noah’s smile became warmer.","\"After all, Ophelia finally apologized to me.\"","Akari was silent for a moment. Then she softly nodded.","\"Hmm... okay.\"","She didn’t push him away. Instead, she simply remained in his arms, quietly holding him back.","Then suddenly she frowned at a thought resurface her. \"But Noah...\"","\"Hmm?\" Noah kept enjoying her hug.","\"We... we didn’t clarify to Ophelia that this all was act, to teach her lesson.\"","Noah’s lips twitched. Then he hug her tightly. \"Let her keep believing that for a little while longer.\""]},{"number":315,"title":"Chapter 315: Dinner [1]","paragraphs":["\"Whistle~ Whistle~\"","Noah whistled happily as he got dressed.","Tonight, a small feast was being held at the Thornveil household to celebrate the happy occasion. Well... at least it was a happy occasion for Noah, his family, Akari, and her father.","The same certainly couldn’t be said for the Thornveil family. Still, as hosts, it was their responsibility to arrange a proper feast and take care of their guests.","Noah slipped into a simple, full-sleeved white shirt and tucked it neatly into a pair of beige trousers. It was nothing fancy. After all, he wasn’t trying to impress anyone tonight.","Once he finished dressing, he picked up his phone, the same phone he hadn’t used in quite some time.","The phone was switched off. he opened it. The moment the screen came to life, Noah was greeted by a flood of missed calls and messages.","\"Wow...\"","He stared at the screen for a moment.","\"I should inform Lyria and Arisha. They must be worried.\"","He quickly sent a message to both of them, assuring them that he was safe and no longer in danger.","Afterward, he noticed several messages from Damien.","Damien had already returned to his village. According to Morgana, he had been extremely worried and even blamed himself for what had happened to Noah.","Fortunately, Morgana had already informed him that Noah had safely returned.","Noah opened the messages.","[Noah!! Are you okay?! What happened to you?!]","[Where have you been?!]","[Thank God you’re safe!! I was so worried! Why is your phone still switched off?! Call me back!!]","[Actually, forget it. I’ll just come visit you!]","[...]","There were several more long messages from Damien. It was obvious that he had been genuinely worried about him.","A smile spread across Noah’s face. \"This bastard is as kind as ever.\"","He shook his head with a helpless smile before putting the phone away. Then he left the chamber. It was already late evening, around 7:30. Noah walked through the corridor toward the dining hall.","As he walked, his thoughts naturally turned toward his current situation.","’My parents are treating me well... Even the animosity between Ophelia and me has finally been resolved.’","He paused internally.","’I could say that everything is going well for me now.’","Yet, strangely enough, that thought made him uncomfortable.","He had barely survived that realm.","He and Akari had faced danger unlike anything he had ever imagined. There had been countless moments when he had genuinely believed they were going to die.","When he had first arrived in this world, he had been exiled from his family. Back then, he had believed they didn’t care much about him.","And, truthfully, he hadn’t cared much about them either. He had been alone. And because he had been alone, there had been no one to worry about.","But now things were different. He had people he cared about. People whose safety mattered to him. People he was afraid of losing.","Noah’s previously cheerful expression slowly became tense.","’What dangers will I have to face in the future? And now that I have people to worry about...’","His hand unconsciously curled into a fist.","’I just hope I won’t lose anyone.’","Everything had returned to normal. His family was reunited.","Akari had returned. Ophelia had apologized. His friends knew he was safe. For once, everything seemed peaceful. And somehow, that peace made Noah even more uneasy.","’Something is bound to happen again.’","He couldn’t shake the feeling. Still, Noah quickly pushed those thoughts aside.","There was no point ruining the evening by worrying about dangers that hadn’t even arrived yet. By the time he reached the dining hall, he had regained his usual expression.","Just then he felt something, he turned around. The huge widow near was opened, cold wind came through it.","He blinked few times, something felt weird. ’Was that my imagination? sigh... my senses are not that strong to sense small movements or dangers... so it must be my imagination.’","He turned back and pushed open the doors and entered.","The dining hall was spacious and elegantly decorated.","At its center stood a long dining table covered with pristine white fabric. Numerous dishes had already been arranged across it, accompanied by various drinks.","The people seated around the table were engaged in casual conversation.","At the head of the table sat Lionel Thornveil. To his left sat his wife, Sofia. Beside her was their son, Liam. Liam was only ten years old.","The young boy had inherited his mother’s brown hair and his father’s emerald-green eyes.","Although he was still too young to form a mana core, he already possessed considerable talent in swordsmanship.","Noah had witnessed his talent himself. And Liam wasn’t only talented with a sword. He also possessed an unusually sharp mind when it came to theoretical studies.","Even at ten years old, he remained remarkably calm and composed for his age.","’Is this what a prodigy looks like at such a young age?’","Noah sighed inwardly.","’He’s already better than Ophelia and me when we were ten. No wonder everyone considers him the future Duke of Thornveil.’","Noah continued toward the table.","On Lionel’s right sat his mother, Lady Elize.","She was around seventy years old, yet she looked closer to fifty, with only a few wrinkles betraying her actual age.","Even in her later years, she still retained traces of the beauty she had possessed in her youth.","Beside Lady Elize sat Noah’s mother, Catelyn.","The Eldritch and Thornveil families had been close friends for generations, so Catelyn and Lady Elize were naturally quite familiar with each other.","Beside Catelyn sat Julian. Nathan sat next to him.","Across the table, beside Liam, sat Ophelia. Next to her was Akari. And at the very end sat Duke Reiji Narukami.","Noah gave everyone a polite bow.","\"Sorry for being late.\"","He then walked toward the only remaining seat and sat beside Nathan.","Unfortunately his seat was directly opposite Duke Reiji.","Noah’s expression twitched.","’Damn. Couldn’t he have taken a seat beside my father or Lady Elize? Why do I have to sit directly across from him?’","He glanced at the imposing Duke. Reiji was calmly sitting there, his presence alone making Noah feel slightly tense.","Noah sighed inwardly.","’Well... there’s no escaping it now.’","He looked down at so many dishes. Not noticing that Duke Reiji was looking at him with observing eyes, before looking away."]},{"number":316,"title":"Chapter 316: Dinner [2]","paragraphs":["Once everyone had settled in and the conversations died down, Lionel stood from his seat. He raised his glass. Everyone gradually turned their attention toward him.","Lionel looked around the table before speaking.","\"Tonight, we have gathered here to celebrate something that we once thought we might never see again.\"","His gaze briefly moved toward Akari.","\"A family reunited, old friend came back, the young man who had been missing for over a month came back.\"","He raised his glass slightly higher.","\"Let us put aside the hardships of the past and enjoy this evening together.\"","A faint smile appeared on his face.","\"To everyone gathered here tonight, welcome.\"","He lifted his glass.","\"Let the feast begin.\"","The others raised their glasses as well. And with that, the small celebration officially began.","---","Thud!","\"Damn! Now this is what I call a proper drink!\"","A loud voice suddenly echoed throughout the dining hall. The speaker was none other than Reiji.","The same man who had appeared cold, composed, and almost intimidating earlier was now laughing loudly, a wide grin plastered across his face as he downed glass after glass of beer.","It was a special brew that had been brought specifically for him. A strong enough drink that even a superhuman like Reiji who was at sovereign core, high stage, could actually taste the alcohol and feel slightly intoxicated.","Noah stared at him for a moment.","’This man really has two personalities.’","One moment, he was as silent and cold as ice. The next, he was as loud and fiery as a raging flame.","’How does someone switch between those two so naturally? Is he bipolar?’","\"Sigh...\" Lady Elize rubbed her temple before speaking. \"Would you mind lowering your voice, Reiji? You are disturbing everyone.\"","Reiji immediately turned toward her. \"Are you ordering me around?\"","He raised an eyebrow before scoffing. \"And do you honestly believe I would listen to you?\"","He slammed his glass onto the table. \"Absolutely not! Tonight is the happiest day I have experienced since my daughter returned to me. I intend to celebrate properly!\"","\"Yes, yes. We have heard you say that several times already.\"","\"Tch!\"","Reiji clicked his tongue. \"You’re simply jealous, you old witch.\"","The corner of Elize’s eye twitched. A vein nearly appeared on her forehead.","She took a slow breath, visibly restraining herself from picking up her glass and throwing it at him.","\"Mother, please let him enjoy himself,\" Lionel said quickly, attempting to prevent the two elders from starting an argument.","Elize merely sighed and returned to her meal.","Meanwhile, Julian turned his attention toward Reiji.","\"Lord Narukami, I must admit, the drink is quite remarkable. And, of course, it is wonderful to see Lady Akari safely returned. From what I have heard, she has already reached the peak of her level.\"","His gaze shifted toward Akari. \"You have truly surpassed us by a considerable margin.\"","Akari smiled politely. \"You flatter me, Lord Eldritch. There is still much for me to learn, and I have a long way to go.\"","Reiji’s chest puffed out proudly. \"Of course! That’s my daughter for you!\"","Akari’s lips twitched slightly. She had already become accustomed to her father’s behavior.","Reiji then turned his attention toward the youngest member of the Thornveil family.","\"Young Liam, how has your training been progressing?\"","Liam immediately straightened his posture.","\"It has been progressing well, Lord Narukami.\"","His answer was polite and composed.","Reiji burst into laughter.","\"Hahaha! Lionel, you have raised your son well. He is remarkably composed for his age, and his mind appears quite sharp.\"","\"I appreciate your kind words, Lord Narukami.\"","Lionel gave a respectful nod.","While the adults continued their conversation, all the younger people at the table silently agreed on one thing. Stay quiet young people.","They lowered their heads and focused entirely on their food.","There was absolutely no reason to involve themselves in whatever conversation the adults were having. it was wise move. Just speak when someone ask anything.","Also It was amusing sight, Akari was going to leave this house but it didn’t put much of tension or bad taste between Thornveil and Narukami family.","Well it doesn’t change much of anything, since Duke Thornveil family already living without her perfectly. Rather it would bring lot of changes on Narukami family.","Noah quietly ate his meal. ’Hope she would become next duchess of eastern Duchy.’ He thought.","However, after a while, he noticed something. His older brother, Nathan, kept glancing at him. He was doing it multiple times.","Finally, Noah looked directly at him.","\"What is it?\"","Nathan immediately looked away.","Noah raised an eyebrow.","\"What?\"","Nathan glanced around the table. No one seemed to be paying attention to them.","Satisfied that their conversation would remain private, Nathan leaned slightly toward Noah and lowered his voice.","\"Noah...\"","His expression became unusually serious.","\"I am asking you this sincerely. What exactly is going on between you and Lady Akari?\"","Noah’s fork suddenly stopped halfway to his mouth.","He froze. For a moment, he simply stared at his brother. Then he slowly swallowed the food in his mouth.","’He noticed...but how?’","Nathan continued watching him expectantly. Noah quietly lowered his fork. This was going to be troublesome.","\"I- I will explain this later. Not now. Not right time.\"","Nathan observed him and then nodded. \"Okay, I expect proper explanation later.\"","Noah nodded.","Then, he glanced at Akari, who was wearing a polite smile as she spoke. From the corner of her eye, she noticed Noah looking at her.","Their eyes met.","Akari raised her eyebrows slightly, as if asking what was wrong.","Noah simply shrugged.","’Sigh... another new trouble. I’ll tell you later.’","It was as if the two of them could understand what the other wanted to say without speaking a single word.","’Sigh... now I’m even more worried about Mother. Last time, when I joked about liking Instructor Morgana, she was furious. And now it’s Akari, who’s around the same age as Mother. Damn... I can’t even imagine what would happen if she finds out.’","Noah found himself facing dangers that weren’t life-threatening, yet were somehow just as terrifying.","Then, once again, he felt something.","His gaze shifted toward the entrance of the dining hall.","’What’s this feeling...? Why do I feel like someone is watching me... or calling out to me?’","He blinked several times, unable to understand the strange sensation."]},{"number":317,"title":"Chapter 317: Into the Woods","paragraphs":["After a while, Noah’s chair slid back as he stood. He looked around the table and said politely, \"I will take my leave. I need some rest.\"","No one tried to stop him. They simply bid him good night as he left the dining hall. As Noah stepped into the corridor, his eyes naturally drifted toward one of the large open windows.","The dining hall was located on the ground floor at the rear of the manor, connected to the main building by a long corridor. Large windows had been placed at intervals along the corridor, allowing the cool night air to flow inside.","Noah walked toward the nearest one and looked outside.","Behind the manor stretched a vast woodland, its lush greenery bathed beneath the pale light of the moon. A gentle breeze passed through the trees, causing the leaves to rustle softly in the darkness.","The sky was not completely clear. Several dark clouds drifted across it, occasionally passing near the moon without completely concealing its light.","\"Moon...\" Noah muttered before sighing.","The gray clouds were a clear sign that the rainy season was approaching. Summer was nearing its end. \"Sigh... The academy should be starting soon.\"","He leaned against the window frame.","\"The semester was already delayed because of all those monsters appearing everywhere.\"","His expression became thoughtful.","What should he do next?","Should he simply focus on training and continue increasing his strength? Or should he join some damn shady organization in order to gather information? Neither option particularly appealed to him.","After staring outside for a while longer, Noah placed one hand on the edge of the window. Then, without hesitation, he jumped out.","Thud!","His feet landed softly on the ground outside.","The woodland immediately surrounded him.","The scent of trees, damp earth, and fallen leaves filled his nose. The forest was considerably darker than the manor grounds, with only fragments of moonlight filtering through the thick canopy above.","Noah looked around.","He wasn’t entirely sure why he had come here. There was simply something that had drawn him into the forest.","Without knowing what compelled him, he began walking deeper into the woodland. He continued for several minutes before eventually arriving at a small clearing.","Noah stopped. A strange feeling suddenly washed over him.","He frowned. \"Huh?\"","He looked around. \"Why did I come here?\"","He stared at the surrounding trees, confusion filling his eyes.","\"What got into me?\"","He couldn’t understand what had compelled him to come all the way here. His expression gradually hardened.","’Was I... being mind-controlled?’","Noah immediately stepped backward.","With a thought, a sword appeared in his hand from his storage ring. His blue eyes darted across the darkness, carefully searching for any trace of an enemy.","Someone had clearly brought him here. But who?","\"Calm down, young man.\"","A woman’s voice suddenly echoed through the forest.","\"I mean you no harm.\"","Noah’s head snapped toward the source of the voice.","From deeper within the forest, a woman slowly walked into the clearing.","She wore a pristine white robe that moved gently with each step.","Her long silver-white hair cascaded down her back, the ends glowing with an orange-red hue that resembled flickering flames.","Her eyes were equally striking, resembling flames burning beneath the moonlight. Her pale skin appeared almost ethereal beneath the soft silver glow of the moon.","Noah was mesmerized by her beauty. Only for a moment.","He quickly regained his senses.","\"Who are you?\"","His voice was tense, his gaze cold and alert.","The woman continued staring at him.","She remained silent for several seconds, her eyes moving slowly from his legs to his hands, then finally to his face.","After inspecting him carefully, she nodded.","\"It appears that you have completely recovered.\"","A small smile appeared on her lips.","Noah’s eyes twitched.","\"Would you care to explain who you are? Or should I—\"","He suddenly stopped.","A memory flashed through his mind.","\"You...\"","His eyes widened slightly.","\"Are you the one who saved Akari and me?\"","He looked at her more carefully.","\"A Phoenix?\"","The woman simply nodded.","\"Yes. I am.\"","She smiled faintly.","\"My name is Sefira.\"","Noah’s tension finally eased.","His sword disappeared, and his posture relaxed slightly.","However, his expression remained cautious.","He bowed lightly.","\"Thank you very much for helping us back there. I do not know how I could ever repay you for what you did.\"","He straightened immediately.","Sefira chuckled softly.","\"You are a good boy.\"","Noah’s lips twitched.","’Good boy?’","He wasn’t sure whether to be annoyed or embarrassed.","\"May I ask why you are here, Ma’am?\"","\"Oh...\"","Sefira hesitated.","\"Hmm...\"","She seemed to think about how to phrase her words.","\"Actually, I wanted to speak with both of you.\"","\"Both of us?\"","\"Yes. You and Akari.\"","Noah narrowed his eyes.","\"Very well. I will call her—\"","\"There is no need.\"","Sefira interrupted him gently.","\"For now, I would like to speak with you alone.\"","Noah paused before nodding.","\"Alright.\"","He remained cautious.","He couldn’t understand why this woman wanted to speak with him privately.","Was there some special reason?","Unfortunately, he had no way of knowing.","All he could do was wait for her to speak.","But as he observed her more carefully, Noah noticed something strange.","The proud woman who had seemed so composed moments ago now appeared...","Restless.","Nervous, even.","Her hand repeatedly clenched and relaxed at her side.","Her eyes occasionally dropped toward the ground, and her lips pressed together tightly before parting again.","Yet no words came out.","’What is making her so nervous?’","Noah continued observing her.","Something was clearly troubling her.","\"Ma’am...\"","His voice finally broke the silence.","\"Is there some problem? You have been standing there without saying anything.\"","\"Huh?\" Sefira was startled. She looked up and met his eyes. She seemed caught off guard. Then her expression gradually became serious.","\"Noah...\"","She took a small breath. \"There is something important I need to tell you.\"","Noah’s expression became slightly more serious. \"What is it?\"","Sefira hesitated again. Her lips parted. \"That...\" She lowered her gaze for a moment at ground.","\"It’s about Mary.\"","The moment that name left her lips, Noah’s eyes widened. His body moved before he could even think. He took a step forward.","\"What about her?\"","His voice was suddenly filled with urgency. \"How do you know Mary?\" He swallowed hard.","\"Are you related to her?\"","Sefira’s expression became complicated. \"Y-yes... I-I am...\"","Her voice trembled slightly.","\"And I—\"","Before she could finish, Noah suddenly bowed deeply.","\"I am extremely sorry.\"","Sefira froze.","Noah’s fists tightened at his sides.","\"It was because of me that she lost her life.\"","His voice trembled.","\"If only I hadn’t insisted on going there...\"","He lowered his head further.","\"She would have been safe.\"","His voice became quieter.","\"She was an orphan. I never knew there was actually someone related to her...\"","Noah slowly raised his head.","His eyes had become slightly watery.","At that moment, he had completely forgotten that the woman standing before him was a Phoenix capable of terrifying power.","\"Who were you to her?\"","He swallowed again.","\"But before that... I am sorry. Truly.\"","His voice cracked slightly.","\"I don’t deserve your forgiveness, but—\"","\"Wait!\"","Sefira immediately interrupted him.","\"Noah, listen to me!\"","Her voice was louder than before. Noah froze. Sefira stared directly into his eyes.","\"Mary is not dead!\"","Silence returned to forest. For a moment Noah didn’t move. His entire body stiffened, As his eyes widened.","\"What...?\" He could barely believe what he had just heard.","Sefira repeated herself, her expression serious.","\"Mary is alive.\"","Noah stood completely frozen. His mind went completely blank.","---","\"Where did Noah go? He was supposed to speak with me and explain what exactly is going on between him and Lady Akari.\"","Nathan muttered as he stepped out of the dining hall.","He took out his phone and decided to call Noah.","Ring!","Ring!","But Noah didn’t answer, even after waiting for a while.","\"Tch... Sigh...\"","Just then, Nathan remembered something.","’Right. Boss said she would be coming here. She wanted to speak with Akari, which means she should be somewhere around the manor.’","At that moment, Akari stepped out of the dining hall.","Nathan’s eyes naturally shifted toward her.","’One by one, everyone is leaving. Well, I suppose it should be the younger ones who leave first. But why is Akari leaving as well?’","Akari noticed him and offered him a small, polite smile.","’Hmm... perhaps Boss is already here and made Lady Akari aware of her presence so they could speak.’ he thought.","Nathan nodded to himself. ’Alright. I will leave for now. Will talk to Noah later.’","He gave Akari a respectful bow before walking away down the corridor. ’But I will definitely find out what’s going on between Noah and Lady Akari.’","He gave Akari a respectful bow before walking away down the corridor. ’But I will definitely find out what’s going on between Noah and Lady Akari.’"]},{"number":318,"title":"Chapter 318: Mary is alive","paragraphs":["\"You’re joking, right?\" Noah asked, disbelief evident in his expression.","Sefira shook her head. \"No. What I am telling you is the truth.\"","Noah didn’t know how to react. Those words couldn’t possibly be true.","He had seen Mary die. He had watched her sacrifice herself and had later seen her body buried beneath the earth with his own eyes. And now, this woman had appeared out of nowhere, claiming that Mary was still alive.","How could he possibly believe that? Noah took a deep breath and forced himself to calm down. He needed to control his emotions before they overwhelmed him.","\"How?\"","His voice was strained.","\"The academy found three dead bodies underground. Mary and two strangers were among them. I saw her die myself... while she was saving me.\"","Sefira folded her arms beneath her chest as she looked at him. The gesture made her chest look more prominent, but Noah’s attention remained fixed entirely on her face and, more importantly on her eyes.","\"...You see, you may already know about Damien—the man blessed by the Sun God. The Child of Heaven, or whatever name you prefer to call him.\"","Noah nodded. \"Yes.\"","He wasn’t particularly surprised that she knew about Damien. Considering that Sefira was clearly a powerful existence, it wasn’t strange for her to possess such information.","Sefira sighed. \"I was tasked with observing Damien, to determine whether he truly was the chosen one.\"","Noah’s expression changed. \"Wait.\" His eyes narrowed suspiciously. \"Do you have some kind of group? An organization?\"","His thoughts quickly connected the pieces. \"And Mary worked for you? Did she come to the academy on a mission?\"","His eyes narrowed further. \"And that day... did she fake her death so she could leave the academy and abandon her entire identity?\"","He paused. \"Wait... was ’Mary’ not even her real name?\"","Noah was once again left completely flabbergasted. ’Seriously... what is this?’ The entire situation was becoming more ridiculous by the second.","\"Well...\" Sefira hesitated. \"You are... somewhat right.\"","Noah took a step back, his gaze dropping toward the ground. ’Mary isn’t dead?’","He clenched his teeth. ’She faked her death, and I was here crying and blaming myself for not being able to save her?’","A surge of anger rose within him. He had considered Mary a close friend. Someone who had sacrificed herself to save his life. But apparently, that entire scene had been an act.","And yet despite the anger burning inside him, there was another emotion he couldn’t suppress.","He felt relief and happiness. She was alive. That was all that truly mattered. Something heavy was lifted from his chest that was like a burden or maybe guilt.","Noah slowly raised his head and looked at Sefira.","She was watching him with a worried expression. She could clearly see that his mood had changed.","\"Where is she?\" His voice was quieter now. At this moment, there was nothing Noah wanted more than to see Mary again.","He wanted to talk to her. He wanted to ask her whether she had ever truly considered him a friend.","Sefira licked her lips nervously before slowly uncrossing her arms.\"N-Noah... I apologize. You must have gone through a lot believing that she was dead...\"","She lowered her gaze. \"I am sorry. This is my fault.\"","Noah stared at her for a moment before sighing. ’Why is this woman apologizing to me?’","Usually, powerful existences like her wouldn’t care much about another person’s emotions. To her, this should have simply been a mission given to Mary, nothing more.","’Perhaps... she really is a kind woman.’","Noah shook his head slightly. \"Well, it must have been you who ordered her to do all this. But if someone wants to apologize to me, then I’d rather hear it from her directly.\"","He looked at Sefira. \"Anyway, forget the apology for now. I just want to meet her.\"","His voice became more urgent. \"Where is she?\"","Sefira blinked. She looked away from him. Her lips moved slightly, but her voice was so small that Noah couldn’t make out the words. \"I... I am Mary...\"","Noah narrowed his eyes. \"Ma’am, I couldn’t hear you. If you don’t mind, could you speak a little louder?\"","Sefira pressed her lips into a thin line. She looked increasingly embarrassed. Then she spoke again. \"That Mary... was me.\"","Her voice was still too low. \"What?\"","Noah leaned forward slightly.","Sefira finally took a breath and shouted, \"I am Mary!\"","Finally he heard and Noah froze.","\"It was me who came to the academy! I was taking the form of that young, nerdy-looking girl using an artifact!\"","She had finally said it. She had finally revealed the truth to Noah. And when Sefira saw the expression on his face.","She couldn’t help but find it somewhat amusing.","\"You are lying, right?\"","\"Why would I? I have no reason to lie to you. It really is me...\"","A silver ring suddenly appeared in her palm. She slipped it onto her finger.","Almost immediately, her appearance began to change.","Her height decreased, her long hair shortened until it rested around her shoulders, and her features shifted. Within moments, the tall, mature woman standing before Noah had disappeared.","In her place stood Mary.","The same young, nerdy-looking girl Noah remembered.","\"This is a concealment artifact,\" she explained, holding up the silver ring. \"It allows me to suppress my powers while disguising myself as someone else. Now, do you believe me—\"","Before she could finish, Noah suddenly kicked off the ground and rushed toward her.","His sword slipped from his hand and fell to the ground with a sharp clang.","Sefira blinked.","She saw him coming, yet she didn’t react. Instead, she simply stood there and allowed him to do whatever he wanted.","Noah threw his arms around her and hugged her tightly.","His strong arms wrapped around her body, pulling her close as her chest pressed against his hard-trained chest. Her cheek rested against the crook of his neck.","\"Mary!! Damn! You’re really alive!\"","He buried his face against the side of her neck, overwhelmed by relief and happiness.","Warmth immediately spread across Sefira’s cheeks.","Noah couldn’t see her expression.","\"N-Noah...\" she muttered awkwardly.","He tightened his embrace.","Despite Sefira’s immense strength, Noah’s hug couldn’t possibly hurt her. However, being embraced so intimately by a man made her far more embarrassed than she had ever expected.","Still, after a moment of hesitation, her arms slowly moved. She wrapped them around Noah as well.","He could feel her palm clutching the fabric of his shirt. \"I’m sorry,\" Sefira whispered. \"I did what I had to do... but I never thought you cared about me this much.\"","\"Well, you’re my friend. Of course I care about you.\"","Noah’s heart beat faster, filled with excitement and happiness.","The memory of watching Mary die was still painfully fresh in his mind. But now that she was standing here, alive and breathing in his arms, the weight that had been sitting in his heart finally began to disappear.","After remaining like that for a long moment, Sefira finally removed the ring.","Her appearance immediately began to change again.","Her body grew taller, her hair lengthened, and her youthful disguise vanished. In moments, she had returned to her original form the mature, incredibly beautiful woman Noah had first encountered.","Yet she was still standing within his arms. He even felt two soft mounds becoming bigger and softer against his chest. That indicated him that she changed back to normal.","Realizing that she had returned to her original appearance, he slowly released her. The two stood face to face.","Sefira was roughly the same height as Akari, towering over Noah slightly.","\"Ma—\"","Noah paused. \"No... Sefira.\"","He didn’t know if could call her friend or not. She was someone still unknown, did she ever thought of him as friend? but she apologize to him. It looked genuine. But for now it didn’t matter.","He looked at her with sudden curiosity.","\"Are you strong?\"","The question was so unexpected that Sefira blinked. A faint blush still lingered on her cheeks, but she proudly lifted her chin.","\"Of course. You could say I’m one of the strongest beings in the world.\"","Noah’s eyes immediately filled with admiration. He stared at her for a moment. His expression now as if he was waiting for this.","His hand clenched into a fist. Without warning, he drove it straight into her stomach with all the physical strength he could muster.","Thud!","The sound of flesh meeting flesh echoed through the forest.","Sefira’s eyes widened slightly in surprise. She hadn’t expected that. But she didn’t stop him.","\"You damn well played with my emotions even if it was for some mission!\"","Noah’s face was filled with anger. He couldn’t tell if she was a good or bad. If she have some bad motive. His other fist came flying forward and struck her stomach again. But right now he was very angry at her.","Thud!","Sefira merely blinked.","For someone like her, Noah’s punches were practically meaningless. They felt as though a child were playfully tapping against her body. For her it felt as if there wasn’t even enough force to kill an ant.","Yet what amused her wasn’t his lack of strength. It was what he was doing. She had never imagined that Noah, of all people, would try to beat her up simply to vent his anger.","A small smile slowly bloomed across her lips. She didn’t stop him. Instead, she simply stood there and allowed him to get it all out of his system."]},{"number":319,"title":"Chapter 319: The Hidden Codex","paragraphs":["\"Enough eavesdropping. Come out.\"","Noah was already calm by now. He turned around to see whom Sefira had been addressing.","From within the woods, his dearest Akari slowly walked into view.","Her eyes were as cold as ice as she stared directly at Sefira.","\"Since when have you been here?\" Noah asked. He hadn’t sensed anyone nearby at all.","For some reason he felt a chill run down his spine.","\"Oh, I just arrived,\" Akari replied calmly. \"I happened to see you hugging her... and then suddenly punching her.\"","Her cold gaze shifted toward Sefira.","\"You called her Mary. So she’s the Mary you told me about, the one who was supposed to have died while saving you?\"","Noah nodded, a soft smile appearing on his face. He was simply relieved and happy that Mary was alive.","\"Yes, she is. As for why she did it, I’ll tell you.\"","Akari raised a hand. As if she didn’t have any wish to hear explanation.","\"No need. You got your Mary back, so congratulations. I don’t need any further explanation.\"","Noah blinked.","Akari lowered her hand. While Sefira didn’t bother much with her reaction and talked.","\"Anyway, let’s put that matter aside for now. I would like to know what actually happened inside that realm.\"","Her voice remained indifferent, but her eyes blazed like flames as they met Akari’s cold.","\"Everything. I want to know everything that happened. Don’t leave out a single detail.\"","Akari raised an eyebrow.","\"Oh? And why should I tell you?\"","She crossed her arms.","\"Yes, you saved us. That’s true. But I still don’t know much about you. Shouldn’t you introduce yourself properly before asking something from us?\"","Sefira let out a small sigh. \"I suppose you’re not wrong.\"","While Akari paused for a moment before continuing.","\"First about those who work for me... there are many. I don’t even know if it would be appropriate to call my group an organization. It began with me gathering information about Monarchs, Gods, and possible events concerning the future.\"","Her tone was surprisingly casual. \"It was originally just me. But over time, it slowly grew.\"","She shrugged.","\"I never gave it an official name, but many of my subordinates have taken to calling it the Hidden Codex.\"","Noah listened carefully to every word.","’She’s not exactly lying... but she’s definitely not telling the whole truth either.’","Even Akari didn’t completely believe Sefira’s explanation.","However, at the moment, she had little choice but to accept it.","Sefira was by no means an unknown existence, even among the world’s strongest beings. Yet Akari hadn’t mentioned her existence to either her father or Lionel after returning and told them that she saved both Noah and her.","That meant she intended to keep Sefira’s existence to herself for now—to understand who she really was and determine whether she could become an ally in the future.","If possible, it would be better to remain on her good side.","\"It seems we’re going to have a long conversation,\" Akari said.","She narrowed her eyes slightly.","\"I’m still not one hundred percent convinced by what you’ve told me. But honestly, I was already expecting you not to reveal your entire history.\"","Noah nodded. \"I think it’s better if we tell her.\"","He glanced at Sefira. \"I... believe in her. And we might be able to learn more through her.\"","His expression became serious.","\"Especially about the Monarchs.\"","He glanced at Akari. \"And even about your new race.\"","Akari sighed. \"You are right, but you really trust her, Noah?\"","Her voice became slightly stricter. \"Don’t forget that she entered the academy using another identity and deceived everyone.\"","Sefira immediately raised an eyebrow.","\"Oh? Are you saying I’m not trustworthy?\"","She looked directly at Akari.","\"First of all, I already explained why I entered the academy. And I have apologized for deceiving you. For your kind information I never apologized so easily, I know I was wrong so I did. Besides, I knew Noah long before you did.\"","Akari’s eyes narrowed. \"Hmph. I know him better than you.\"","She folded her arms. \"I spent seven months with him. Just the two of us, trapped in that world.\"","Sefira’s expression immediately changed. Her brows furrowed, as if she looked slightly displeased from her reply.","Noah couldn’t understand why her mood had suddenly changed.","But then he remembered how jealous Akari had become when she thought Noah was getting too close to her daughter.","’No way...’","\"Cough!\"","Noah deliberately coughed, trying to draw their attention.","Both women immediately turned toward him at the same time.","Noah flinched. ’Why do I suddenly feel like I’m standing between two predators?’","Someone like Noah who was still far away in strength compare to Sefira and Akira.","It was still unbelievable to think that they might be seeing him differently, and not just as friend or disciple.","Though he could understand Akira being jealous. But Sefira also?","For now he dismissed the possibility of Sefira having similar kind it feelings for Noah.","And whether it was love or not. He couldn’t decide.","\"Listen, ladies. We should talk about this calmly.\"","He looked toward Sefira.","\"I also want to learn more about the Monarchs, if possible. So I hope you’ll tell us what you know.\"","\"Yes. I will.\"","Sefira nodded without hesitation.","Akari stared at the two of them for a moment before letting out another sigh.","\"Fine. I’ll tell you.\"","She looked at Sefira.","\"I’ll explain what happened to me and how I ended up trapped inside that realm.\"","Noah immediately understood why Akari had agreed so easily.","As suspicious as she was of Sefira, Akari valued knowledge even more.","If Sefira truly possessed information about Monarchs, Gods, and the future, then refusing to listen would be foolish.","\"Yes,\" Noah added. \"Later, I’ll tell you everything from my side as well.\"","Akari started to tell her everything from start. Every detail, without leaving anything.","Later Noah explained everything from his side once Akari was done.","---","[A/N: Hello guys! Sorry for not updating for the past two days. I’m currently on vacation, so I’ve decided to take a break for the rest of this week and enjoy some time off.","I’ll try to upload a Chapter sometime in the middle of the week if possible, but honestly, it’s unlikely. 😂","I’ll be back to my regular Chapter uploads from September 21st.","Sorry for the sudden break, and thank you for your patience! ❤️]"]},{"number":320,"title":"Chapter 320: Well, at least we’ve learned something about them","paragraphs":["Only Noah and Akari remained in the forest now. Sefira had already left after hearing everything they had to say.","Before leaving, she had also shared some information she knew about the Monarch of Decay, as well as the ancient dragon who had most likely been responsible for trapping Akari inside that realm.","In Noah’s and Akari’s hands were small orange-colored orbs.","They were communication devices Sefira had given them so they could contact her whenever necessary.","Akari clenched the orb in her hand. \"Chaos Dragon? Monarch of Destruction?\"","She sighed and rubbed her temples. \"And why did the ancient Storm Dragon have to be an enemy of Decay? This whole situation is a mess.\"","Noah stored his orb inside his storage ring. \"Well, at least we’ve learned something about them.\"","\"Yes, but there’s still one thing I can’t understand.\"","Akari’s expression became serious. \"Why did he do it? Why did the Dragon of Destruction trap me inside that realm and then create a way for Damien to enter it as well?\"","Noah was thinking about the same thing. He rubbed his chin, trying to piece together everything they had learned.","His knowledge from reading novels was surprisingly useful in situations like this, even if the circumstances were completely different from the stories he had read.","\"Hmm... I do have one theory.\"","Akari immediately looked at him.","\"What is it?\"","\"You remember what happened at the end, right? I used the Moon Goddess’s divine power and completely destroyed Decay’s puppet... or whatever that thing actually was.\" He said while rubbing his chin.","\"Yes. And?\" She raised her one brow and asked.","\"If I hadn’t been there, it would have been Damien who used the Sun God’s divine power to destroy it.\"","Akari nodded. \"Yes... but what does that have to do with anything?\"","Noah narrowed his eyes as he organized his thoughts. \"This is just speculation, but...\"","He paused, then continued with soft exhale. \"Maybe that Chaos Dragon wanted Decay to become aware of your existence.\"","Akari’s expression changed slightly.","Noah continued. \"As Sefira said, Decay is weak against divine power. So even though his true body wasn’t there, destroying his puppet with divine power should have caused some kind of damage to him.\"","He frowned then. \"Even if it wasn’t physical damage, something must have been affected.\"","Akari thought for a moment. \"Perhaps his soul?\"","Noah’s eyes widened. \"Exactly. It have very high chances to be true...\"","He then frowned again. \"But why?\"","He looked at Akari. \"According to Sefira, the Monarch of Destruction should be stronger than the Monarch of Decay. So why would he need us to damage Decay instead of killing him himself?\"","Akari fell silent. After thinking for a few moments, she finally spoke.","\"Perhaps he doesn’t want Decay dead.\"","Noah raised an eyebrow. \"Then what does he want?\"","\"Maybe he wants to weaken him...\"","Akari slowly pieced together the possibility. \"And then have someone else finish him off. For what purpose, though... or maybe something else entirely...\"","She sighed. \"I don’t know. There are too many unknowns.\"","Akari rubbed her temples again. \"I think we need to research this more carefully. Sefira did say that she would tell us more once she learned more herself.\"","Noah nodded. \"Yeah. For now, that’s probably all we can do.\"","The two fell silent, both lost in thought. The more they learned about the ancient beings involved. The more complicated everything became.","Cold night wind moved though the forest, rustling the numerous leaves of woodland.","Noah remained there thinking deeply about Sefira.","Akari noticed the conflicted expression on Noah’s face.","\"You’re happy that the friend you thought was dead is still alive.\"","Noah pressed his lips into a thin line before slowly nodding.","\"But... I...\"","\"But now you can’t trust her,\" Akari finished for him.","Noah sighed and ran a hand through his white hair.","\"Yeah. She’s not Mary. She’s Sefira. As happy as I am to know that Mary is still alive... I’m even more suspicious now. I don’t know whether she’s genuinely on our side or if she has some ulterior motive and is simply using us.\"","\"Hmm... But she revealed her true identity to you. And you still don’t trust her?\"","\"She might have done that so I would lower my guard and tell her everything.\"","Akari thought about it for a moment before speaking.","\"She’s definitely strong enough to force information out of you if she wanted to. And I actually think she possesses some kind of mind-control ability.\"","\"Huh?\"","Noah’s eyes widened slightly.","\"Yeah... you’re right. I didn’t come here because I was being controlled.\"","\"Exactly. I felt her trying to influence me as well, but my mental fortitude was strong enough to resist it. Still, I could sense where she wanted me to go... so I came here.\"","\"Damn. That woman is seriously strong...\"","Noah frowned.","\"I really don’t think we should trust her just yet. We need to be more cautious around her.\"","Akari nodded in agreement.","\"Yeah. I think that’s the safest choice for now.\"","She then suddenly flicked Noah on the forehead.","\"Now, let’s go back. It’s already late.\"","\"Ow... Okay.\"","Noah rubbed his forehead before following Akari back toward the manor.","---","The two eventually emerged from the woodland and quietly entered the manor through the same window Noah had used earlier.","Before they went their separate ways, Noah turned toward her.","\"Akari, good night.\"","\"Good night.\"","She replied with a soft, beautiful smile.","It was an unusually gentle smile.","Noah grinned. \"Well, I hope you have some sweet dreams about me.\"","He couldn’t resist teasing her. To his surprise, Akari chuckled softly, covering her mouth with one hand. Her eyes curved into crescent shapes as she smiled.","\"Sure. Sweet dreams involving you are always welcome.\"","She turned around and walked away.","Noah stood there completely stunned. A faint blush crept across his cheeks. \"Damn... she got me this time.\"","He let out an awkward laugh before turning around and leaving as well.","---","Meanwhile, outside the manor, several meters away from the window through which Noah and Akari had entered, someone was hiding behind one of the trees at the edge of the woodland.","The figure slowly stepped out from the shadows.","He had blond hair and violet eyes. It was Nathan. His expression was one of pure astonishment.","\"L-Lady Akari... and Noah... came out of the woods together... this late at night?\"","Nathan’s mind was struggling to process what he had just witnessed.","\"Noah wasn’t in his room, so I came looking for him...\"","And then, by sheer coincidence, he had stumbled upon Noah emerging from the woodland with Akari.","The two had been standing surprisingly close to each other.","Nathan’s face gradually turned pale.","\"M-Mother is going to faint if she finds out about this!\" He clenched his fists. \"Noah, you bastard!!\""]},{"number":321,"title":"Chapter 321: Departure","paragraphs":["It was morning.","It was finally time for Noah to leave the city, return home with his family, and then head back to the academy. Classes would resume on Monday, so there was little time left to linger.","Noah was already dressed and ready to leave. The last two nights had felt strangely empty.","After becoming accustomed to sleeping beside Akari for months, sleeping alone again had made him realize just how much he had gotten used to her presence.","’Does she feel the same way?’","Noah wondered.","He left his chamber and made his way toward the entrance of the manor, where everyone had already gathered.","The entire Thornveil family was there, along with Akari and her father, Reiji Narukami.","Noah’s own family stood nearby as well. Julian, Nathan, and Catelyn Eldritch.","However, for some reason, his elder brother was staring at him with an unusually sharp gaze.","Nathan’s violet eyes practically felt like daggers.","Noah had absolutely no idea why his brother was looking at him like that.","’What did I do this time?’ He decided not to think too much about it.","\"Good morning, everyone.\"","Noah gave a light, polite bow.","Akari smiled gently when she saw him.","\"Looks like everyone is ready. We can leave now.\" Julian spoke before turning toward Duke Lionel, who stood a short distance away.","Beside Lionel stood his current wife, Sofia, their son Liam, and Ophelia. Lady Elize, Lionel’s mother, stood nearby as well.","Ophelia would remain in Thornveil City for the time being, while Akari would return to the Eastern Duchy with her father.","Interestingly, Noah had also learned that there was a high possibility of Akari becoming the next Duchess of the Eastern Duchy. She told it to her father that she wanted to be.","Of course, nothing had been decided yet. The matter still needed to be discussed among the members of the Narukami family, their ministers, and other important figures before a final decision could be made.","Julian stepped forward. \"Thank you, Your Grace, my friend Lionel. Your boundless hospitality has honored us greatly.\"","Lionel laughed. \"It was my pleasure to honor you and extend my hospitality once again, Julian. The same goes for you, Lord Reiji. I hope we will have another opportunity to gather like this in the future.\"","\"Indeed.\" Reiji nodded. \"I would like that as well. However, for now, we should return. We each have our own territories to manage.\"","His cold, stern expression was completely different from the loud and boisterous Duke who had been drinking at the feast the previous night.","That man was nowhere to be seen.","The person standing before them now was once again the proud and formidable Duke of the Eastern Duchy.","Sofia elegantly bowed, lightly lifting the edge of her gown. \"We would be deeply honored to welcome you and your houses to our halls again whenever your travels bring you this way. Have a safe journey.\"","Noah looked toward Ophelia and gave her a small nod.","She returned it. And with that, they finally left the manor.","A long, spacious carriage had been prepared to take both families to the teleportation gateway station in Everhold City.","The interior was considerably larger than Noah had expected. It had a spacious seating area with seats facing one another and a small wooden table positioned between them.","Julian, Nathan, and Catelyn sat on one side.","Reiji, Akari, and Noah sat on the other.","Noah naturally chose the seat beside Akari.","The journey to the station was mostly silent. No one spoke much, and the quiet atmosphere settled over the carriage.","There was only one thing troubling Noah. He was going to part ways with Akari. He quietly glanced at her from the side.","Her face had healed considerably since they escaped the realm. Her complexion had returned to its former beauty, and if anything, the ordeal seemed to have made her appear even more beautiful.","Her dark-blue hair was neatly tied up as usual, while her sharp blue eyes remained focused ahead.","The dark-blue fabric of her kimono suited her perfectly.","’Haah... When will I get to see her again?’","Noah sighed internally. ’I really don’t want to leave her.’","He had spent months with Akari. They had fought together, survived together, and even slept beside each other.","Somehow, he had become far more attached to her than he had realized.","’I really did get too attached to her over these past few months.’","Perhaps sensing his gaze, Akari turned her head.","Her blue eyes met his. She tilted her head slightly.","Noah immediately realized that she understood what he was feeling.","A soft smile appeared on her lips. \"I will miss you, Noah.\"","She said it openly, without caring that everyone else in the carriage could hear her.","No one commented on it.","They all knew the two of them had been trapped together for months. They had fought side by side and survived countless dangers together.","It was only natural that they had grown close. \"And I will come to visit you from time to time, if that does not bother you.\"","Those words eased Noah’s sadness somewhat.","He smiled and nodded. \"Of course. It would be my honor if Lady Akari wished to visit me.\"","He paused before adding with a playful smile, \"And who knows? Perhaps next time, I should address you as Duchess.\"","Akari chuckled. \"Haha. It isn’t that simple.\"","\"Indeed.\" Reiji suddenly joined the conversation with a loud laugh.","\"I still have sons. She will have to deal with them before she can take my position.\"","Julian nodded in agreement. \"That is true. But considering how much Akari has grown, I believe she could handle it.\"","\"Perhaps,\" Akari said.","\"But first, I need to relearn many things—political affairs, administration, and managing the territory itself. I have been away for too many years, and I have lost some of the skills I once possessed.\"","\"You will regain them quickly, Lady Akari,\" Catelyn said respectfully.","\"Yes, Mother. I know she will.\"","Noah’s cheerful response earned him another sharp glare from Nathan. He felt a sudden chill run down his spine.","’Why is he still looking at me like that?’","---","Eventually, they arrived at the gateway station.","Numerous teleportation portals stood throughout the enormous facility, each leading to a different destination.","Both the Narukami and Eldritch families stood together for their final farewells.","\"It was a great honor meeting you and sharing a dinner with you, Duke Narukami,\" Julian said.","\"The honor was mine.\" Reiji nodded. \"We shall meet again.\"","His gaze shifted toward Noah. \"Young man, I hope to see you even stronger the next time we meet.\"","\"I certainly will be.\"","After exchanging their final farewells, Noah’s family turned toward their designated portal.","Reiji headed toward his own.","Akari followed her father for a few steps before suddenly stopping.","She turned around.","Noah was already looking at her. He smiled and raised his hand.","\"Bye!\"","He said it in a cheerful voice.","Akari couldn’t help but chuckle. She raised her hand and waved back at him.","Then she turned around and walked toward her portal.","Noah watched until she disappeared. He slowly exhaled. ’Well... we’ll meet again eventually.’","A faint smile appeared on his face.","’Now, I should get going too.’","\"Noah!\"","His mother’s voice suddenly called out. \"What are you doing? Come on!\"","Noah turned around.","\"Coming!\"","He quickly ran toward his family. With that, his brief stay in Everhold City finally came to an end.","Now it was time to return to the academy. And, more importantly. It was time to meet his friends again.","---","[A/N: I am back!! Sorry for the wait!!]"]},{"number":322,"title":"Chapter 322: Back To Home","paragraphs":["\"Nancy!! I missed you so much!\"","Noah immediately scooped the soft black cat into his arms and pulled her tightly against his chest. He rubbed his cheek against the top of her head with an overly affectionate grin.","\"Meow! Meow!\"","Nancy struggled desperately against the clingy human who had suddenly returned after being gone for more than a month.","\"Goodness, why are you struggling so much?\" He looked genuinely offended. \"Don’t you miss me?\"","Before Nancy could answer or, more accurately, before she could escape Noah began showering her head with kisses.","\"Meow!!\"","Nancy pushed her tiny paws against his face, desperately trying to create some distance between them. Her golden-yellow eyes narrowed as she stared at him.","If Noah had understood cat language, he would have clearly heard:","NOOOO! ENOUGH IS ENOUGH! HUMAN!","Unfortunately for Nancy, Noah understood absolutely nothing. And so, the assault of affection continued.","\"You’re still as cute as ever.\"","\"Meeoow!\"","Nancy’s ears flattened. Her eyes practically screamed for help. Fortunately for her, a prince charming arrived to save her.","\"I think we should have a talk, brother.\"","Noah suddenly stopped. He slowly turned his head toward the doorway.","Nathan was standing there, leaning against the doorframe with his arms crossed over his chest.","His violet eyes were fixed on Noah with an expression that made him look less like an older brother and more like an investigator who had finally caught his suspect.","Noah blinked. ’Why does he look at me like I’ve committed a crime?’","Nathan raised an eyebrow.","Noah slowly released Nancy. The moment her paws touched the floor, she sprinted out of the room without looking back.","Noah watched her disappear. \"Tch! she ran away because of you.\" Then he looked back at his brother. \"Big bro, what do you want to talk about?\"","Nathan uncrossed his arms and walked into the room. He stopped directly in front of Noah. \"You damn well know what I want to talk about.\"","Noah’s smile stiffened.","Nathan stared at him. \"What’s your relationship with Lady Akari?\"","Noah’s expression immediately froze.","\"Ah...\" He took a small step backward. \"Haha... Brother, you mean...\" A nervous laugh left his mouth.","Nathan didn’t even blink. \"Yes.\"","His voice was calm, but his expression said he had already decided Noah was guilty. \"What’s going on between you and Lady Akari?\"","Noah swallowed. ’He really isn’t going to let this go.’","\"Brother, she’s my master.\"","He tried to sound casual. \"She taught me for months while we were trapped in that realm. Naturally, we became closer.\"","Nathan stared at him for several seconds. \"That’s it?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"Do you honestly think I’m an idiot?\"","Noah’s smile disappeared.","Nathan sighed and rubbed his forehead. \"The way you look at her isn’t how a disciple looks at his master.\"","He narrowed his eyes. \"And I saw the two of you coming out of the woods last night. You were not in chamber so I tried to search for you and then saw it.\"","\"What?!\"","Noah’s eyes widened. His face instantly became awkward. ’He saw us?’","He quickly tried to think of an excuse. But the expression on Nathan’s face made one thing painfully clear.","There was no point lying. Noah sighed and dropped his shoulders.","\"Okay... I’ll tell you.\"","Nathan’s expression softened slightly.","\"But promise me you won’t tell anyone.\" Noah looked at him seriously. \"Especially Mother.\"","Nathan’s lips twitched. He could already imagine Catelyn’s reaction if she discovered what her son was thinking.","\"Fine.\" He nodded. \"I promise. Whatever you tell me stays between us.\"","Noah relaxed. He sat down on the edge of the bed.","Nathan walked over and sat beside him.","Noah remained silent. He rubbed the back of his neck awkwardly.","\"You see...\" He hesitated. \"I don’t really know how to explain it. I think...\" Noah stared at the floor. \"I think I like her.\"","Nathan didn’t respond. He simply stared at his younger brother. His expression slowly changed from curiosity to disbelief.","He had suspected something like this. But hearing Noah actually admit it was another matter. \"...You actually like her?\"","Noah gave an embarrassed smile. \"Yeah.\"","Nathan remained silent for another moment.","Then Noah continued. \"But I definitely feel attached to her. And I’m attracted to her too.\"","His voice became more serious. \"I care about her... probably more than I realized. He lowered his gaze. \"But is it really love?\"","He shook his head. \"I don’t know. I’ve never been in love before, so how am I supposed to know?\"","Nathan looked at him thoughtfully. \"You loved Ophelia before. The daughter of the woman you’re currently crushing on.\"","Noah’s face immediately twisted with embarrassment. \"Haha...\"","He rubbed the back of his neck. ’Damn, now I feel ashamed. But this is not like me, I should be more open.’","\"I don’t think what I felt for Ophelia was love.\"","Nathan raised an eyebrow.","\"No?\"","\"I think it was mostly attraction.\"","Noah sighed. \"Maybe even an obsession. I was attached to the idea of being with her.\"","His expression became more thoughtful. \"But what I feel for Akari is different.\"","He leaned backward, placing both hands against the mattress. His eyes drifted toward the ceiling. \"With her... I actually care about her happiness. I worry about her. When she’s in danger, I can’t just sit there and do nothing.\"","A faint smile appeared on his lips. \"And when we were trapped in that realm together...\" He paused. \"She had become to very important to me before I realized.\"","Nathan listened quietly.","Noah’s expression then became uncertain. \"But I don’t know what she thinks about me.\"","He turned his head slightly. \"She cares about me too. A lot, actually. She’s even willing to put her life on the line for me.\"","His brow furrowed. \"But I don’t know what kind of feelings she has for me.\"","Nathan stared at him for a moment before letting out a long sigh. \"You really are something, little brother.\"","Noah glanced at him. \"What?\"","Nathan shook his head with a mixture of amusement and disbelief. \"You’re actually falling for a woman around our mother’s age.\"","Noah winced. \"Don’t say it like that.\"","Nathan laughed quietly. \"If Mother finds out, she’s going to lose her mind.\"","Noah sighed.","\"Yeah...\" He gave a teasing smile. \"But what can I do?\"","Nathan chuckled. \"At least you’re aware of how ridiculous this situation sounds.\"","\"I know.\" Noah scratched his cheek. \"I can’t exactly control who I develop feelings for.\"","Nathan nodded. \"Fair enough.\""]},{"number":323,"title":"Chapter 323: Talk with Nathan","paragraphs":["Nathan leaned back slightly. \"So what are you planning to do?\"","\"What do you mean?\"","\"Are you going to tell Lady Akari?\"","Noah became silent. After a moment, he shook his head. \"Not yet.\"","Nathan frowned slightly.","\"Why?\"","\"Even if I become certain that this is love...\" Noah’s expression became serious. \"I still wouldn’t confess right away.\"","Nathan studied his brother’s face.","Noah clenched his fist lightly.","\"She’s too strong.\" His voice carried a hint of determination. \"I need to reach a level where I’m at least somewhat close to her strength.\"","He looked down at his hand. \"Only then will I feel confident enough to stand before her and tell her how I feel.\"","Nathan remained silent for a moment.","Then a small smile appeared on his face. He stood up from the bed. \"Well, if that’s what you want, then I’ll respect it.\"","Nathan turned toward the door. \"And don’t worry. I’ll keep your little secret.\"","Noah chuckled. \"Thanks, bro.\"","Nathan paused and looked back at him. \"But honestly...\" A teasing grin appeared on his face.","\"I think you’ve already figured out how you feel. You’re just too embarrassed to admit it.\"","Noah’s coughed. \"It’s really embarrassing, dude.\"","Nathan laughed. \"Sure, sure.\"","He waved his hand dismissively. \"Anyway, I should go. You need to start packing. You are heading back tomorrow for academy.\"","He reached the doorway before remembering something. \"Oh, and Father asked you to visit him in his study. He wants to hear more about what happened to you.\"","Nathan’s expression became slightly more serious.","\"So don’t keep him waiting.\"","\"Sure. I’ll go see him.\"","Nathan nodded. Then he suddenly looked back at Noah with a suspicious expression.","\"And one more thing.\"","Noah raised an eyebrow.","\"What?\"","\"Don’t bring too much trouble back with you.\"","Noah stared at him.","Nathan sighed. \"For some reason, I have a feeling you’re going to bring an even bigger disaster into our family than before.\"","Noah’s mouth twitched. \"Tch! Have some faith in me.\"","He placed a hand against his chest. \"I’ll handle everything. And I swear I won’t cause any more problems.\"","Nathan gave him a deeply skeptical look. \"Yes, yes. You swear.\"","He shook his head. \"You were always troublesome, that habit still haven’t gone away.\"","With that, Nathan left the room. The door closed behind him.","Noah remained sitting on the edge of his bed. Then his thoughts drifted back to what they had just discussed.","Akari and his feelings for her. A smile appeared on his face.","And then Arisha and Lyria. Noah’s expression slowly became complicated.","\"Hmm.\"","He rubbed his chin. \"Maybe I won’t bring that many problems.\"","He paused. \"...Just tiny problems... Yeah.\"","He nodded to himself with complete seriousness.","\"Just tiny problems...\"","Unfortunately, even Noah didn’t sound particularly convinced.","Later Noah went to his father’s study and talked with him for hours before coming back to chamber. then packed things for academy, putting them in storage ring.","He also got few calls from his friends, he only send them message, let’s talk when we meet.","---","Somewhere far away from Noah’s home, in a luxurious room illuminated by the faint glow of moonlight, two figures were engaged in a quiet conversation.","\"You finally decided to add a new member to our cult?\"","The voice belonged to a young man with black hair. His sharp grey eyes were fixed on the man sitting casually on the edge of the window.","The other man wore a black suit and a dark mask that concealed most of his face. His short black hair was slightly tousled, and despite his relaxed posture, there was something unsettling about his presence.","He was Shadow. And tonight, he was speaking with one of his subordinates, Kaelan Nightfall.","\"Yes, but not yet.\"","Kaelan frowned. \"Then when?\"","He couldn’t help wondering when Shadow planned to bring this mysterious person into their so-called cult and, more importantly, who exactly this person was.","\"Hehe~ After the end of your second semester at the Academy. During the winter vacation.\"","Kaelan, who was sitting comfortably in a chair, crossed his arms. \"Okay... then why are you telling me this right now?\"","\"Because before we bring that person into our cult, we need him to obtain something.\"","Shadow tilted his head slightly. \"And you’re going to help him get it.\"","Kaelan stared at him suspiciously. \"So, can you at least tell me who this person is? The one you want to bring into our cult... and the person you want me to help?\"","\"Haha. You already know him.\"","Shadow’s voice carried a hint of amusement.","\"His name is Noah Eldritch.\"","Kaelan’s eyes widened.","\"W-What?! Noah?\"","He immediately sat up straight. \"But he’s been missing for an entire month!\"","Shadow casually waved his hand. \"Don’t worry. He’s back.\"","Kaelan remained frozen for a moment. \"He’s... back?\"","\"Yes.\" Shadow leaned against the window frame. \"After all, I was the one who indirectly helped him return. You’ll see him at the Academy soon enough.\"","\"How do you kn—\" Kaelan suddenly stopped himself. He let out a tired sigh and rubbed his forehead.","\"Forget it. You always seem to know things somehow.\"","He shook his head before looking at Shadow again. \"So, where was he? Where did he go missing? And what exactly do you want me to help him find?\"","\"As for where he was...\" Shadow shrugged. \"I don’t know.\"","Kaelan stared at him in silence. Of course, he knew Shadow wasn’t actually incapable of answering. He simply didn’t want to tell him.","After dealing with Shadow for so long, Kaelan had learned that trying to pry information out of the masked man was usually a complete waste of time.","He decided not to press the matter. \"Fine. Whatever.\"","Kaelan leaned back in his chair. \"Then tell me what I’m supposed to help him find.\"","Shadow remained silent for a few seconds. The relaxed atmosphere suddenly became slightly heavier.","\"As for what you need to help him find...\"","He paused. A faint smile appeared beneath his mask.","\"Hehe~ You’ll find out when the time comes.\"","Kaelan’s expression twitched.","\"Of course...\" Once again, Shadow had given him an answer without actually answering anything.","’This bastard really enjoys keeping everyone in the dark.’","But there was one thing Kaelan knew for certain. Whatever Shadow wanted Noah to obtain, it was definitely not going to be ordinary."]},{"number":324,"title":"Chapter 324: Back to Academy","paragraphs":["\"I’m back here again.\"","Noah stood before the massive gates of Novaris Academy, staring at the familiar sight before him.","For a moment, he simply stood there.","The towering gates, the elegant academy buildings visible beyond them, the familiar atmosphere filled with students and mana... Everything looked exactly as he remembered.","Nancy was resting comfortably on his shoulder, completely uninterested in his surroundings. The black cat merely curled herself against him as if the entire academy meant absolutely nothing to her.","Noah smiled faintly. He was genuinely happy to be back.","Yet, somewhere deep inside, another part of him desperately wished he could turn around, go home, crawl into his bed, and never step foot inside this damn academy again.","Unfortunately, fate or rather, his circumstances had other plans.","He had no choice but to attend.","’Tch. What kind of transmigrator am I supposed to be?’","Noah sighed inwardly.","’I need to start doing something. I can’t keep stumbling into dangerous situations without understanding what’s happening around me. There are too many hidden dangers in this world.’","His expression became slightly more serious.","’And if I want to uncover those dangers, I have to stay close to Damien...’ He grimaced. ’Even if that’s the last thing I want to do.’","With that reluctant thought, Noah walked through the academy gates.","As he entered, he couldn’t help but glance around.","The beautiful academy welcomed him back with its familiar scenery. Students were scattered throughout the grounds, some returning from their homes, others carrying luggage toward their dormitories.","It was Sunday afternoon, and Noah still needed to officially register his return.","So, after entering the academy, he headed directly toward the administration building.","The staff there were visibly surprised when they saw him.","News of Noah’s disappearance had spread throughout the academy long ago. Even though he had been exiled from his family, he was still the son of Duke Eldritch. Moreover, his performance at the academy had been impressive, especially during several dangerous incidents.","His disappearance had naturally attracted plenty of attention.","After completing the necessary procedures, Noah regained access to his dormitory.","He returned to his room and began arranging his belongings.","Nancy, however, had absolutely no interest in helping.","The moment Noah placed her down, the black cat casually stretched before climbing onto his bed. She curled herself into a comfortable ball and immediately prepared to sleep.","Noah stared at her.","\"Huh... You really are a lazy cat.\"","He shook his head with a helpless smile.","\"Sleep well. I’ll go outside and meet my friends. I’ll bring something delicious for you when I come back.\"","\"Meow~\"","Nancy replied lazily without even opening her eyes.","Noah sighed. \"Yeah, yeah. Go to sleep.\"","He left the room. A short while later, Noah arrived at the academy cafeteria.","Since it was already afternoon, the cafeteria was filled with students having their lunch. The lively atmosphere immediately reminded Noah of his normal days at the academy.","\"Noah!!!\"","A familiar male voice suddenly rang out.","Noah turned around.","A young man with short black hair was rushing toward him, weaving through the returning students without the slightest concern for anyone in his path.","It was Damien.","Noah’s lips curved into a genuine smile when he saw him.","Damien’s expression was filled with relief, and his eyes even looked slightly teary.","Noah felt touched. Then his smile disappeared.","’Wait...’ His eyes widened. ’He’s going to hug me!’","\"No, no, no!\" Noah immediately raised both hands toward Damien. \"Hey! Wait! Don’t come any closer!\"","Unfortunately, Damien wasn’t listening. If anything, Noah’s warning seemed to have the opposite effect.","Damien planted his foot against the ground with even greater force and lunged forward.","\"This bastard!\"","Noah’s instincts kicked in. He might have been emotional, but he wasn’t weak.","His reflexes had improved tremendously, and although Damien was faster, Noah’s reaction speed was enough to deal with a simple charge.","He swiftly sidestepped.","Damien’s arms closed around nothing. His momentum carried him forward.","\"THUD!\"","He crashed onto the floor. The surrounding students turned toward them.","Noah stared at Damien with a mixture of horror and disbelief.","\"Bro! I understand that you’re emotional and happy to see me alive and back at the academy...\"","He pointed at Damien accusingly.","\"But don’t come charging at me like you’re trying to hug me!\"","Damien slowly pushed himself up onto his knees.","\"Sniff...\"","He looked at Noah with watery eyes.","\"Noah you are safe. I’m so happy!\"","Noah’s expression softened. \"Yeah, I know, buddy. It’s good to see you again.\"","Damien wiped his eyes. \"Yes, I was so worried. I thought something had happened to you because of me\"","\"Noah!\"","A gentle female voice suddenly interrupted him.","Noah instantly turned his head. A beautiful young woman was approaching them.","She carried an aura as warm and comforting as sunlight itself. Her long golden hair was tied into a single braid that rested over her right shoulder, giving her an elegant and mature appearance. Her unique pink eyes were filled with both worry and relief.","It was Lyria. The kind and gentle angel of the academy.","The moment she saw Noah standing safely before her, the worry in her expression slowly gave way to relief.","Noah stared at her. ’Is she going to hug me too?’ Before he even realized what he was doing, his body reacted on its own.","His arms slowly spread open.","Lyria approached hurriedly and then stopped. She stared at Noah’s outstretched arms with a slightly confused expression.","Noah froze.","\"...\"","Lyria blinked.","\"...\"","Noah slowly realized how ridiculous he looked.","\"Tch. The first thing he expects after coming back is a hug from a girl.\" Another familiar voice came from behind Lyria. \"That’s Noah for you.\"","Noah turned his head.","A beautiful young woman with long violet hair and striking yellow eyes stood behind Lyria. Her arms were crossed beneath her chest, and with an indifferent expression.","It was Arisha.","Noah immediately lowered his arms.","\"Arisha...\"","She gave him a faintly amused look.","\"Welcome back.\"","From the side, Damien had already gotten back onto his feet.","\"You didn’t accept my hug, though.\"","Noah immediately glanced at him.","\"Like hell I’m going to accept a hug from another man!\"","Damien looked genuinely offended. \"What’s wrong with hugging your friend?!\"","\"Everything!\"","Noah ignored his complaint.","Lyria shook her head helplessly before turning her attention back to Noah.","\"Well, putting that aside...\"","Her expression softened.","\"I’m really happy that you’re back safely, Noah.\"","She stepped a little closer, her eyes still filled with concern. \"Where have you been? I was so worried when I heard that you had gone missing.\"","Noah scratched the back of his head awkwardly.","’Damn... She’s a real saintess.’","\"Well... it’s a long story.\" He gave her an apologetic smile. \"But I’m back safely now. I’m sorry for making all of you worry.\"","\"I knew Noah would come back.\"","A confident voice came from behind them. Leonard approached with a huge grin on his face. His tanned skin and blond hair were as familiar as ever.","\"You’re someone who can face danger head-on and survive it.\"","He gave Noah a firm pat on the shoulder. \"Still, I’m glad our Noah is finally back.\"","Arisha let out a small sigh of relief. \"We’re all glad you’re safe.\"","Noah smiled. \"Thanks, everyone.\"","A short distance away, another familiar figure stood quietly.","Kaelan, their eyes met. He simply gave him a small nod.","\"Welcome back.\"","Noah returned the gesture.","\"Thanks.\"","Seeing all of them gathered together again gave Noah a strange feeling.","For the past month, he had been separated from the academy and everyone he knew here. Now, standing among his friends once again...","It felt strangely comforting. The group had finally been reunited.","Noah looked around.","’But... where are Draven and Regnar?’","As if answering his question, he suddenly spotted the two familiar figures nearby.","A smile immediately formed on his face. He raised his hand and waved toward them. And just like that, the group was truly together again."]},{"number":325,"title":"Chapter 325: Tell Me Truthfully...","paragraphs":["The 200-centimeter-tall giant opened his enormous arms wide. \"Noah! My friend!\"","It was Draven Rockbane.","Noah’s expression immediately stiffened. ’Damn! He’s going to crush me with that hug!’","He instinctively tried to step backward. Unfortunately for him, Arisha was standing directly behind him.","Before Noah could react, she casually placed a hand against his back and pushed him forward.","\"Hey!\"","And just like that, Noah stumbled straight into the arms of the barbarian giant.","\"Hehe~\"","Arisha chuckled quietly as she watched him get caught. Two enormous arms wrapped tightly around Noah. Noah froze for a moment.","’Huh?’","He had expected to feel like he was being squeezed by a bear. But surprisingly, ’Well, it’s not that tight.’","Despite Draven’s enormous physique and naturally powerful body, his cultivation was actually lower than Noah’s.","Noah was currently at the peak of the High Stage of the Condensed Core Realm, while Draven was only at the Low Stage.","So although Draven was physically imposing, Noah was more than capable of handling the pressure of his embrace.","Draven happily patted Noah’s back. \"I knew you’d come back!\"","He laughed heartily. \"I heard from Ragnar that you had gone missing. You were even on television!\"","Noah’s eye twitched. ’Why my news airing on TV? can’t do anything about it.’","He quickly pulled himself out of Draven’s embrace. \"It’s good to see you too, Draven. And hello, Ragnar. How have you two been?\"","Beside them stood Ragnar, a tiger-type beastman who somehow looked more like a giant cat than a tiger.","He nodded. \"We’ve been doing well. But what about you? Where have you been all this time?\"","\"It’s a long story.\" Noah gestured toward the cafeteria.","\"Let’s go eat first. I’ll tell you guys everything while we’re having lunch.\"","Damien, who had been watching the entire exchange, suddenly frowned. \"You let him hug you? Then what about—\"","\"You bastard! You’re starting to sound gay!\" Noah immediately cut him off.","Leonard, who was standing beside Damien, suddenly took a step away from him. \"Well... he does kind of sound like one.\"","He glanced at Damien cautiously. \"I should probably be careful around him.\"","\"Fuck both of you.\" Damien glared at them.","Noah looked at Leonard. Leonard looked back at Noah. A brief silence passed between them.","Then Noah’s eyes widened. \"Damn... Do you want to fuck?\"","Leonard’s expression changed. \"Noah...You were thinking the same thing.\"","Noah immediately pointed at Damien. \"Damn! It’s confirmed. Damien is gay!\"","\"You bastard!!\" Damien’s face flushed with anger.","Lyria, who had been listening to the conversation, immediately blushed. \"Guys! Don’t say such dirty word!\"","She tried to stop them, looking increasingly embarrassed. The others couldn’t help but laugh.","A short while later, the group settled around one of the cafeteria tables, their lunch plates spread out before them.","Noah, as usual, took the seat between Arisha and Lyria.","Nobody questioned it. They had long since become accustomed to this arrangement.","Noah always ended up sitting between the two girls.","Whenever Arisha refused to give him a seat beside her, Noah would simply keep bothering her with pointless questions and nonsense until she eventually surrendered with a defeated sigh.","So, over time, this had simply become normal.","Arisha glanced toward him.","\"Now, dear boy...\" Her voice was soft as she turned toward Noah. She was sitting at left side. \"Care to explain where you’ve been? It made us so much worried.","Noah could see her worry behind those yellow eyes.","If anyone else had called him \"dear boy,\" Noah probably would have beaten shit out of them.","But Arisha, Akari, Lyria And perhaps Sefira they were exceptions. Also his mother.","Across the table, Damien leaned forward. \"Yes! Tell us! I want to know too!\"","Kaelan and Leonard were seated beside him, with Ragnar nearby. Draven had taken the seat beside Lyria, who was sitting on Noah’s right.","Noah looked around the table. \"Well, then. Let me explain.\"","He paused before continuing. \"I assume you guys already heard about how Damien and I entered the labyrinth and how I ended up getting trapped inside an unknown portal?\"","Everyone nodded. Noah then began explaining what had happened.","He told them about becoming trapped inside an unfamiliar realm and eventually encountering Ophelia’s mother, Akari. There was no real reason for him to hide her return.","Sooner or later, the news would spread anyway.","The servants at the Thornveil estate had already seen Akari. Once the servants started talking, the information would eventually spread throughout the manor, then Everhold City, and eventually beyond.","That was simply how rumors worked. So Noah decided there was little point in keeping her return a secret from his closest friends.","However, he carefully left out several crucial details. He didn’t reveal that Akari was a dragon. He didn’t tell them about the strange difference in the flow of time inside the realm.","And, most importantly, he didn’t mention the Monarch he had encountered.","Instead, Noah explained that a powerful monster had appeared, and after a difficult battle, they managed to defeat it and escape the realm.","Of course, when describing the battle, Noah made sure to emphasize just how difficult it had been. He couldn’t help but make himself sound a little cooler.","Once he finished explaining, Draven let out a low whistle.","\"Noah...\"","He looked at him with genuine admiration.","\"You really are a man.\"","Draven gave him an approving nod.","\"Even though you weren’t particularly powerful at the time, you still tried to save a lady while facing such a dangerous monster even when she was far stronger than you. My respect for you has increased.\"","Noah nodded solemnly.","\"Thank you.\"","The others also began complimenting him and expressing their relief that he had survived.","Damien, however, looked somewhat guilty.","\"Noah... I’m sorry. It was because of—\"","\"Hey, don’t apologize.\" Noah interrupted him. \"It’s already in the past. Your apology isn’t going to change what happened.\"","He smiled. \"Besides, I ended up getting the chance to learn from Lady Akari. That was a huge opportunity for me.\"","Even Damien couldn’t argue with that. \"Still... it must have been difficult.\"","Lyria gently placed her hand on Noah’s right shoulder. Her expression was filled with genuine concern.","Noah felt a warm sensation spread through his chest. Her simple gesture made him feel strangely comforted.","He smiled. \"Yeah... it was difficult.\"","However, while everyone else was talking, Arisha remained silent. She wasn’t eating. She simply stared at Noah.","Her yellow eyes remained fixed on his face, as if she were trying to look beyond his words and determine whether he was hiding something.","Kaelan, who had been quietly eating, eventually noticed her unusual behavior. \"Is something on your mind, Arisha?\"","Noah’s wide smile faded slightly. He turned toward her.","\"Something happened?\"","Arisha nodded. Her yellow eyes narrowed slightly as she studied him. Then she asked calmly, \"Is Lady Akari a beautiful woman?\"","Noah blinked. That was an unexpectedly strange question. Still, he answered honestly. \"Yes.\"","A proud smile appeared on his face. \"My master is extremely beautiful.\"","Arisha’s expression didn’t change. \"Then tell me honestly...\"","She leaned slightly toward him. \"How much did you flirt with her?\"","The entire table fell silent as everyone froze.","Noah’s body stiffened. ’What?!’ His mind went completely blank. But he quickly regained his composure.","He couldn’t let Arisha see that the question had struck too close to the truth.","So he forced a confused smile onto his face. And, surprisingly, his acting was excellent.","Even Noah himself was impressed.","Unlike when he had tried to lie to his brother, Nathan, about his feelings for Akari, he somehow found it much easier to deceive Arisha.","\"What are you talking about?\" He spoke with an almost offended expression. \"My relationship with Lady Akari is purely that of a master and disciple.\"","He shook his head solemnly. \"Our bond is as pure as holy water.\"","He looked directly at Arisha. \"So please don’t make such inappropriate comments about it.\"","Arisha continued staring at him. Her expression didn’t change even slightly.","Noah’s smile remained on face ’She doesn’t believe a single word I just said.’"]}]);
